00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:25.484
<i>Dinosaurs are in our world.</i>


00:01:25.519 --> 00:01:27.486
<i>And with every confrontation,
we learn more</i>


00:01:27.521 --> 00:01:29.489
<i>about this frightening
new reality.</i>


00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.828
<i>How did we get here?</i>


00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.395
Oh, my God.


00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:37.129
<i>It's been three decades</i>


00:01:37.164 --> 00:01:39.132
<i>since the deadly events
at Jurassic Park,</i>


00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.168
<i>and we've yet to find a way
for these animals</i>


00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.170
<i>to live safely among us.</i>


00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.438
<i>After the devastating eruption</i>


00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.640
<i>of Isla Nublar's
long-dormant volcano,</i>


00:01:46.674 --> 00:01:50.210
<i>those who survived were
transported to the mainland.</i>


00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.879
Many of the larger predators
were captured,


00:01:52.914 --> 00:01:55.314
but the remaining creatures
scattered here


00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.784
in Big Rock National Park.


00:01:57.819 --> 00:01:59.820
While most remained in the wild,


00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.555
<i>those who made their way
to civilization</i>


00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.891
<i>struggled to adapt
to unfamiliar conditions.</i>


00:02:03.924 --> 00:02:07.929
<i>Local authorities have warned
the animals are unpredictable</i>


00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:11.198
<i>and, when hungry,
extremely violent.</i>


00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.768
<i>As the dinosaurs spread
across borders,</i>


00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.902
<i>a global black market has</i>
<i>risen.</i> -They're not ours.


00:02:15.937 --> 00:02:18.740
Go on, you sad, pathetic loser!


00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:21.675
<i>To combat the growing
threat of illegal poachers,</i>


00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:24.343
<i>the U.S. Congress awarded
sole collection rights</i>


00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:27.548
<i>to the global giant
Biosyn Genetics.</i>


00:02:27.581 --> 00:02:30.349
At Biosyn, we're dedicated
to the idea


00:02:30.384 --> 00:02:34.454
that dinosaurs can teach us
more about ourselves.


00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:38.324
<i>CEO Lewis Dodgson
has created a sanctuary</i>


00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:41.260
<i>in Italy's Dolomite Mountains,
where he hopes to study</i>


00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:43.497
<i>the dinosaurs'
ancient immune systems</i>


00:02:43.531 --> 00:02:45.667
<i>for unique
pharmaceutical properties.</i>


00:02:45.699 --> 00:02:47.634
<i>While Biosyn believes
we can handle</i>


00:02:47.668 --> 00:02:50.805
<i>genetic power responsibly,
the public remains skeptical.</i>


00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.608
<i>Some note that these
government contracts have led</i>


00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.877
to massive spikes
in Biosyn's profits.


00:02:56.911 --> 00:02:59.413
And rumors persist
of a human clone


00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:03.250
who mysteriously disappeared,
leading to a worldwide search.


00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.352
<i>Some believe she's
genetically identical</i>


00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.420
<i>to Charlotte Lockwood,
deceased daughter</i>


00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:10.525
<i>of Jurassic Park cofounder
Benjamin Lockwood.</i>


00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.728
<i>Now that we've brought these
animals back from extinction...</i>


00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.431
<i>Are we responsible for them?</i>


00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:20.501
<i>Or should they be left
to fend for themselves?</i>


00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.704
<i>As we adapt to
an ever-changing world,</i>


00:03:23.737 --> 00:03:26.406
<i>we must find answers
to these questions...</i>


00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.644
<i>for their safety
as well as for our own.</i>


00:04:09.683 --> 00:04:14.454
We are inside
the illegal breeding facility.


00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:18.658
The juveniles are kept in cages
to keep costs down.


00:04:18.692 --> 00:04:20.894
It's medieval.


00:04:24.531 --> 00:04:26.399
Claire.


00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.807
Why do you think
he's separated from the rest?


00:04:34.608 --> 00:04:37.476
I don't think
he's gonna make it.


00:04:41.882 --> 00:04:43.784
No. What are you doing?


00:04:43.817 --> 00:04:44.985
We can report this.


00:04:45.019 --> 00:04:47.721
The DFW takes days
to investigate.


00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:50.057
We can save this one now.


00:04:51.526 --> 00:04:52.826
It's okay. It's okay, buddy.


00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.697
Okay. Here we go.


00:05:02.002 --> 00:05:04.071
Nope. No!


00:05:04.105 --> 00:05:06.406
Lift.


00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.576
- Support the head.
- Yeah.


00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.744
Okay. Yeah.


00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.682
Okay, come on.
Come on, let's go.


00:05:20.721 --> 00:05:22.757
- Hold on.
- To what?


00:05:46.581 --> 00:05:48.983
Claire, we're gonna get shot!


00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.456
- No. Claire, no! No, Claire!
- Oh, no!


00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:07.634
Oh, shit.


00:06:11.004 --> 00:06:12.471
Everybody good?


00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:14.507
No!


00:06:25.019 --> 00:06:28.088
Okay. Okay, so I think
we get this one to the DFW,


00:06:28.122 --> 00:06:29.790
and then we hit them again.


00:06:29.824 --> 00:06:32.692
Yeah. Yeah, you saw
that breeding ground, right?


00:06:32.726 --> 00:06:34.528
We're done.


00:06:36.197 --> 00:06:37.764
I got a call last week.


00:06:37.798 --> 00:06:38.865
It's a real job.


00:06:38.899 --> 00:06:41.468
Something I could do
to effectively change things.


00:06:41.502 --> 00:06:43.603
- I got to take it.
- They need us.


00:06:43.637 --> 00:06:45.906
Are you saving these dinosaurs
because they need us,


00:06:45.939 --> 00:06:47.908
or are you saying them
to absolve yourself?


00:06:47.942 --> 00:06:49.509
Claire.


00:06:49.543 --> 00:06:51.745
I mean, this is crazy. We...


00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.146
Claire.


00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:54.848
You're doing the right thing.


00:06:54.882 --> 00:06:58.019
But this... this isn't the way
to go about it anymore.


00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:00.922
Honestly, you need someone


00:07:00.954 --> 00:07:02.656
who's good at being shot at.


00:07:02.689 --> 00:07:05.959
Aren't-aren't you and Owen
still, like, a weird thing?


00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:07.528
It's not that weird.


00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.064
- He didn't mean weird. No.
- Mm-mm.


00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.699
Uh, he meant, like, surprising.


00:07:32.586 --> 00:07:34.588
Hyah!


00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:53.841
Let's bring 'em home! Hyah!


00:08:14.928 --> 00:08:16.963
Hyah!


00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.924
No.


00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.039
Okay. Come here.


00:09:02.676 --> 00:09:04.778
Okay.


00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.626
We're gonna get you
someplace safe.


00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:24.697
Hey.


00:09:28.235 --> 00:09:31.672
There you go. There you go.


00:09:32.373 --> 00:09:33.908
Yeah.


00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.753
Hey.


00:12:34.421 --> 00:12:36.256
Where you been?


00:12:36.289 --> 00:12:37.390
Nowhere.


00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:39.860
What are you burning?


00:12:39.893 --> 00:12:43.264
Oh, nothing.
Just some old blankets.


00:12:44.965 --> 00:12:46.866
You sure you didn't
go past the bridge?


00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:48.878
That's the look you give me
when you think I'm lying.


00:12:48.902 --> 00:12:51.004
- Well, are you?
- No.


00:12:51.038 --> 00:12:53.082
Maisie, you're literally
looking everywhere but here.


00:12:53.106 --> 00:12:55.576
I said I didn't
go past the bridge.


00:12:59.446 --> 00:13:01.081
Maisie.


00:13:01.115 --> 00:13:03.317
- Can we start over?
- I know, Claire.


00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.294
There are people out there
who'll do anything to find me.


00:13:05.318 --> 00:13:06.953
I'm not angry.


00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:08.822
So that means
you don't have to be angry.


00:13:08.855 --> 00:13:10.356
I'm not angry.


00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.924
I can take care of myself.


00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:13.561
Hey.


00:13:13.595 --> 00:13:16.196
It's okay for us
to depend on each other.


00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.032
That's what people do.


00:13:18.065 --> 00:13:20.134
How would I know what people do?


00:13:20.167 --> 00:13:23.102
The only people I've spoken to
in the past four years


00:13:23.136 --> 00:13:25.172
are you both.


00:13:25.205 --> 00:13:28.341
Besides, I'm not even
a real person anyway.


00:13:28.375 --> 00:13:29.375
What?


00:13:29.409 --> 00:13:31.578
I was made from someone else.


00:13:31.613 --> 00:13:34.181
I'm not me.


00:13:40.988 --> 00:13:43.956
You're the only you
who ever was.


00:13:45.192 --> 00:13:46.393
What?


00:13:46.427 --> 00:13:47.995
No.


00:13:48.028 --> 00:13:49.530
Was that, like, really corny?


00:13:49.563 --> 00:13:50.864
It was so corny.


00:13:50.898 --> 00:13:52.231
Can we keep that between us?


00:13:52.265 --> 00:13:53.567
Can't promise that.


00:14:00.341 --> 00:14:01.609
- Hey, kid.
- Hi.


00:14:01.643 --> 00:14:03.277
Sorry I'm late.


00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:04.578
Bop, bop.


00:14:06.113 --> 00:14:06.980
Aw.


00:14:07.014 --> 00:14:08.414
You smell like horses.


00:14:08.448 --> 00:14:09.551
Mm.


00:14:09.583 --> 00:14:11.018
Oh, you like that, do you?


00:14:11.051 --> 00:14:12.318
- I do, yeah.
- Aw.


00:14:12.352 --> 00:14:13.386
Okay.


00:14:13.419 --> 00:14:15.022
Um...


00:14:15.054 --> 00:14:17.625
I'm gonna... make dinner.


00:14:17.658 --> 00:14:19.493
Everything okay?


00:14:20.961 --> 00:14:23.129
She went into town again.


00:14:24.398 --> 00:14:25.999
This kid.


00:14:26.033 --> 00:14:28.101
Did you talk to her?


00:14:28.134 --> 00:14:29.970
I tried.


00:14:31.437 --> 00:14:32.972
I'll talk to her.


00:16:12.306 --> 00:16:13.707
All right.


00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.342
Cut away from yourself.


00:16:20.447 --> 00:16:21.548
Whoa.


00:16:21.582 --> 00:16:22.683
Whew.


00:16:22.716 --> 00:16:24.751
- Stone-cold.
- Right?


00:16:24.786 --> 00:16:26.587
I would not mess with her.


00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.388
No way.


00:16:34.094 --> 00:16:35.471
Listen, kiddo,
we should probably talk


00:16:35.495 --> 00:16:36.563
about you going into town.


00:16:37.731 --> 00:16:39.099
I don't think you understand


00:16:39.131 --> 00:16:40.409
how bad it is
being trapped here.


00:16:40.433 --> 00:16:42.034
You're not trapped here.


00:16:42.068 --> 00:16:43.504
We just don't trust people.


00:16:43.538 --> 00:16:45.072
No, you just don't trust me.


00:16:45.105 --> 00:16:47.407
And then you expect me
to trust you.


00:16:47.441 --> 00:16:50.244
- Why can't I have any freedom?
- Because you can't.


00:16:55.148 --> 00:16:57.384
That went great.


00:16:57.417 --> 00:16:59.152
What is happening?


00:16:59.754 --> 00:17:01.755
- She's 14.
- Yeah.


00:17:01.788 --> 00:17:04.124
You remember what that was like.


00:17:04.726 --> 00:17:06.528
I do.


00:17:07.595 --> 00:17:09.530
We can't keep her here forever.


00:17:09.564 --> 00:17:11.198
If we don't figure this out,


00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.133
she's gonna go a lot farther
than the bridge.


00:17:13.165 --> 00:17:14.845
If they find her, we're never
gonna see her again.


00:17:14.868 --> 00:17:16.538
We got to protect her.
That's our job.


00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:17.771
That's what we're gonna do.


00:17:17.805 --> 00:17:19.540
Protect her how?


00:17:19.574 --> 00:17:21.576
By locking her inside?


00:17:22.442 --> 00:17:25.112
<i>She's got questions.</i>


00:17:25.813 --> 00:17:28.080
<i>You know,
questions we can't answer.</i>


00:17:29.717 --> 00:17:31.618
<i>She wants to know who she is.</i>


00:17:34.354 --> 00:17:37.457
<i>Who Charlotte Lockwood was.</i>


00:17:42.596 --> 00:17:44.364
Tracked Grady to his house.


00:17:44.397 --> 00:17:48.670
You were right...
the raptor's got a juvenile.


00:17:49.604 --> 00:17:52.204
But listen,
there's something else.


00:17:52.874 --> 00:17:55.342
I found that girl
you've been after.


00:18:09.723 --> 00:18:11.424
Here you go.


00:19:23.765 --> 00:19:25.198
Thanks for coming.


00:19:25.231 --> 00:19:27.535
Wasn't sure who to call.


00:19:27.567 --> 00:19:29.604
Fish and Wildlife
didn't even want to see it


00:19:29.636 --> 00:19:30.971
if it wasn't a dinosaur.


00:19:31.005 --> 00:19:33.272
Yeah, well,
they get all the attention.


00:19:33.306 --> 00:19:34.942
You guys want to vary
the sampling plots


00:19:34.976 --> 00:19:36.410
a hundred yards each?


00:19:36.442 --> 00:19:38.846
- These your students?
- Yeah.


00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.447
We've been looking
into the impact


00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:42.683
of industrial farming
on the environment,


00:19:42.717 --> 00:19:44.951
so this is right up our alley.


00:19:44.986 --> 00:19:47.855
They hit 60 fields
in the county.


00:19:47.888 --> 00:19:49.891
Have you seen anything
like this before?


00:19:49.923 --> 00:19:51.858
No. Not like this.


00:19:51.893 --> 00:19:55.295
They've been leaving degraded
fields all across the Midwest.


00:19:55.327 --> 00:19:58.700
First, these big companies
try to kill off all the insects.


00:19:58.732 --> 00:20:00.667
Now this.


00:20:10.711 --> 00:20:11.979
Is that your land?


00:20:12.012 --> 00:20:13.446
That's the Bennetts' corn.


00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:14.715
The locusts didn't eat that.


00:20:14.749 --> 00:20:17.483
You plant the same seed
as the Bennetts?


00:20:17.518 --> 00:20:18.920
No.


00:20:18.952 --> 00:20:21.221
We are independent.


00:20:21.989 --> 00:20:24.391
They use Biosyn seed.


00:20:26.358 --> 00:20:28.461
Yeah, I bet they do.


00:20:29.362 --> 00:20:31.330
You say you caught a live one?


00:20:40.775 --> 00:20:43.242
Okay. Let her down slow.


00:20:44.077 --> 00:20:47.548
- Got it?
- Yeah. Easy.


00:20:53.887 --> 00:20:55.623
Why do we dig?


00:20:55.655 --> 00:20:58.893
'Cause paleontology is science,


00:20:58.925 --> 00:21:01.494
and science is about the truth,


00:21:01.528 --> 00:21:03.698
and there is truth
in these rocks.


00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:05.265
Grant!


00:21:07.366 --> 00:21:08.903
You're gonna want to see this.


00:21:21.413 --> 00:21:22.849
Ellie Sattler.


00:21:24.585 --> 00:21:26.385
Alan Grant.


00:21:26.419 --> 00:21:28.088
You look the same.


00:21:28.122 --> 00:21:30.090
Oh.


00:21:30.124 --> 00:21:33.460
And this place... it's so...


00:21:34.095 --> 00:21:36.530
...so, uh, you.


00:21:37.898 --> 00:21:39.534
I'm sorry, I...


00:21:39.567 --> 00:21:41.769
If I'd known you were coming,
I would've...


00:21:43.738 --> 00:21:44.771
Uh...


00:21:47.642 --> 00:21:49.644
Can I get you something?
A beer or...


00:21:49.676 --> 00:21:52.814
Um, well, maybe not
at 10:00 a.m.


00:21:52.846 --> 00:21:54.714
But iced tea or...


00:21:54.749 --> 00:21:56.116
Tea. Yeah.


00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:57.785
Tea. I can do that.


00:21:59.153 --> 00:22:01.588
Saw a lot of tourists
on the way in.


00:22:02.522 --> 00:22:04.724
Well, the funding's dried up,
so...


00:22:04.759 --> 00:22:06.693
somebody's got to pay
for all this.


00:22:06.727 --> 00:22:09.328
Right. Thank you.


00:22:10.631 --> 00:22:13.067
I read your articles
about soil science


00:22:13.099 --> 00:22:14.769
and regenerative farming.


00:22:14.801 --> 00:22:16.703
- It was great.
- Thanks.


00:22:16.737 --> 00:22:19.372
Gave me grounds for some hope,
for a change.


00:22:19.405 --> 00:22:20.775
How are your kids?


00:22:20.807 --> 00:22:22.676
Mm.


00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:24.443
Amazing. Grown.


00:22:24.477 --> 00:22:26.445
It's shocking.
They're both in college.


00:22:26.479 --> 00:22:27.914
Can you believe that?


00:22:27.949 --> 00:22:29.650
And Mark?


00:22:31.417 --> 00:22:33.621
It's over.


00:22:33.653 --> 00:22:35.589
Oh.


00:22:36.523 --> 00:22:38.391
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.


00:22:38.424 --> 00:22:39.926
It's okay.


00:22:39.961 --> 00:22:41.662
I'm back to me.


00:22:41.695 --> 00:22:42.730
My work.


00:22:42.762 --> 00:22:44.932
- You know, it's...
- That's great.


00:22:44.965 --> 00:22:46.733
It's good. It is.


00:22:46.767 --> 00:22:48.035
I'm alone at last.


00:22:48.068 --> 00:22:49.569
Exciting times.


00:22:49.604 --> 00:22:52.138
Yeah, I'm living
the Alan Grant life.


00:22:52.173 --> 00:22:53.974
- It's just...
- Can be lonely.


00:22:54.008 --> 00:22:55.675
...so free.


00:22:58.144 --> 00:22:59.913
Ellie...


00:23:00.981 --> 00:23:05.619
You didn't come out all this way
just to catch up, now, did you?


00:23:09.123 --> 00:23:11.025
Well, it's a locust.


00:23:11.057 --> 00:23:14.161
Mandibles, wings, thorax, but...


00:23:14.194 --> 00:23:16.462
God, the size of it is massive.


00:23:18.031 --> 00:23:21.067
It has genes that have been
extinct since the Cretaceous,


00:23:21.102 --> 00:23:23.203
and swarms of them
are decimating crops


00:23:23.237 --> 00:23:24.971
from Iowa to Texas.


00:23:25.006 --> 00:23:27.008
Terrifying, right?


00:23:27.974 --> 00:23:29.609
Started as a few hundred.


00:23:29.644 --> 00:23:31.778
There could be millions
by the end of the summer.


00:23:31.811 --> 00:23:33.445
If they keep going,


00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:36.116
there will be no grain
to feed chickens, cattle.


00:23:36.150 --> 00:23:38.184
The entire food chain
would collapse.


00:23:38.219 --> 00:23:42.823
Well, it's clearly designed,
but why would anyone do that?


00:23:43.723 --> 00:23:47.795
None of the crops they're eating
are Biosyn seed.


00:23:47.827 --> 00:23:49.461
Biosyn.


00:23:49.496 --> 00:23:50.998
You're saying Biosyn made this.


00:23:51.031 --> 00:23:52.833
I mean, it would not shock me


00:23:52.866 --> 00:23:55.468
that they want to control
the world's food supply.


00:23:55.502 --> 00:23:57.939
Not before a few million starve.


00:23:57.971 --> 00:23:59.507
Yeah, what is that saying?


00:23:59.539 --> 00:24:02.042
Uh, we're three meals away
from anarchy?


00:24:02.076 --> 00:24:06.047
If we don't stop them, you can
pick your last three meals.


00:24:07.548 --> 00:24:09.583
So why are you
bringing it to me?


00:24:09.616 --> 00:24:11.251
I need concrete evidence


00:24:11.285 --> 00:24:13.520
Biosyn's responsible
for all this.


00:24:13.554 --> 00:24:15.155
I need to go to their sanctuary


00:24:15.189 --> 00:24:17.857
and get DNA
from another locust there.


00:24:19.125 --> 00:24:21.895
But I need a witness.


00:24:21.929 --> 00:24:23.064
Alan.


00:24:23.964 --> 00:24:26.200
You command respect.
People believe you.


00:24:26.232 --> 00:24:28.234
Ellie.


00:24:28.269 --> 00:24:30.171
You know why I'm here?
It's quiet.


00:24:30.203 --> 00:24:31.705
I'm done with all that.


00:24:31.739 --> 00:24:33.874
Are you? Okay.


00:24:33.907 --> 00:24:35.608
Well, I'm sorry, Alan.


00:24:35.643 --> 00:24:37.778
Nobody gets that luxury anymore.


00:24:37.811 --> 00:24:39.180
Not even you.


00:24:39.212 --> 00:24:41.182
And you know what?


00:24:41.214 --> 00:24:42.983
You're the one I trust.


00:24:47.855 --> 00:24:51.125
This Biosyn sanctuary is what,
a hundred miles from anywhere?


00:24:51.157 --> 00:24:52.859
How do you even get in there?


00:24:52.893 --> 00:24:54.228
I got an invite.


00:24:54.260 --> 00:24:56.730
From their in-house philosopher.


00:24:57.565 --> 00:24:58.766
Seems there's a lot of money


00:24:58.798 --> 00:25:00.800
in being a chaotician
these days.


00:25:00.835 --> 00:25:04.538
And he just happened to invite
you out of the blue, huh?


00:25:05.271 --> 00:25:06.941
He said there were things
I'd want to see.


00:25:06.973 --> 00:25:08.075
Uh-huh.


00:25:13.713 --> 00:25:15.682
You coming or what?


00:25:30.663 --> 00:25:31.942
Every animal captured
on the mainland


00:25:31.965 --> 00:25:33.601
comes through here
before shipping out


00:25:33.634 --> 00:25:34.845
to Biosyn's sanctuary
in the Dolomites.


00:25:34.868 --> 00:25:36.703
We give them medical attention


00:25:36.737 --> 00:25:39.006
and make sure
they leave healthy.


00:25:39.039 --> 00:25:41.041
So much security.


00:25:41.075 --> 00:25:42.675
Those are just the ones you see.


00:25:42.710 --> 00:25:45.078
A lot of shady types out there
want these guys.


00:25:47.615 --> 00:25:49.215
Your plane's just fueling up.


00:25:50.217 --> 00:25:52.819
Biosyn's a tough invite.
You guys must know somebody.


00:25:52.853 --> 00:25:54.989
- Do you mind if I...?
- Of course.


00:25:56.790 --> 00:25:58.291
Hello.


00:25:58.325 --> 00:25:59.926
You see me?


00:25:59.960 --> 00:26:01.194
Follow me.


00:26:01.228 --> 00:26:02.930
We rescued these guys


00:26:02.962 --> 00:26:05.075
from an illegal breeding farm
in Nevada a few weeks ago.


00:26:05.098 --> 00:26:07.233
Shut the whole place down.


00:26:07.268 --> 00:26:08.669
Anonymous tip.


00:26:08.701 --> 00:26:10.203
Good girl.


00:26:10.237 --> 00:26:12.373
Yes. Yes.


00:26:12.405 --> 00:26:14.340
Alan.


00:26:14.375 --> 00:26:16.777
You never get used to it.


00:26:17.377 --> 00:26:19.212
- Take care.
- Thank you.


00:26:19.246 --> 00:26:20.980
- Bye.
- Okay.


00:26:57.151 --> 00:26:58.419
Hey.


00:27:00.153 --> 00:27:02.655
You look just like Blue.


00:27:05.358 --> 00:27:07.327
This?


00:27:07.361 --> 00:27:09.696
You want to try it?


00:27:10.297 --> 00:27:11.765
Okay.


00:27:19.906 --> 00:27:21.174
Huh.


00:27:25.179 --> 00:27:27.181
Maisie, don't move.


00:27:31.050 --> 00:27:32.153
Hey, girl.


00:27:33.220 --> 00:27:34.387
Staying out of trouble?


00:27:34.421 --> 00:27:36.990
She had a baby.
That's impossible.


00:27:39.292 --> 00:27:40.728
Back up.


00:27:40.760 --> 00:27:42.429
She won't hurt us, right?


00:27:42.462 --> 00:27:44.164
Oh, you're damn right she will.


00:27:44.198 --> 00:27:45.732
Just breathe.


00:27:45.766 --> 00:27:47.401
If you don't,
she'll think you're scared.


00:27:47.433 --> 00:27:49.068
I am scared.


00:27:49.103 --> 00:27:52.105
Nah. She doesn't
need to know that.


00:27:58.979 --> 00:28:00.847
Her nest has got to be nearby.


00:28:00.881 --> 00:28:03.183
- Maisie, get inside.
- I'm coming with you.


00:28:03.217 --> 00:28:04.785
What did I just say?


00:28:14.194 --> 00:28:15.496
We got to move.


00:28:15.529 --> 00:28:17.298
Not yet. We need the girl.


00:28:19.365 --> 00:28:20.467
Hey, what's up?


00:28:20.500 --> 00:28:21.969
Oh.


00:28:24.837 --> 00:28:27.974
Maisie? Maisie.


00:28:31.778 --> 00:28:34.080
Mm-mm. Mm-mm.


00:28:34.114 --> 00:28:35.148
Where are you going?


00:28:35.182 --> 00:28:36.317
You can't keep me here.


00:28:36.349 --> 00:28:37.851
You're not my mother.


00:28:43.390 --> 00:28:45.992
She's leaving the house.


00:29:12.419 --> 00:29:14.221
- Tie it down!
- Come on, let's go.


00:29:19.192 --> 00:29:21.261
Let's get out of here!


00:29:39.614 --> 00:29:41.781
Who are you?


00:30:02.604 --> 00:30:04.305
Claire!


00:30:05.271 --> 00:30:06.940
- They found her.
- What?


00:30:06.973 --> 00:30:08.442
- Who are they?
- Poachers.


00:30:08.474 --> 00:30:10.009
I've seen 'em around.


00:30:10.044 --> 00:30:11.345
Leader's a real shit heel.


00:30:11.377 --> 00:30:14.114
He must have recognized me,
followed me here.


00:30:14.147 --> 00:30:15.915
- Where is she?
- Go get the truck.


00:30:15.949 --> 00:30:17.817
Oh, my God.


00:30:20.287 --> 00:30:21.922
Oh, God.


00:30:23.590 --> 00:30:25.593
Owen.


00:30:25.626 --> 00:30:27.493
Hey. No.


00:30:31.464 --> 00:30:33.299
They took her kid, too.


00:30:37.270 --> 00:30:39.540
I am gonna get her back.


00:30:39.574 --> 00:30:41.407
I promise you that.


00:30:51.519 --> 00:30:52.952
Come on.


00:30:52.986 --> 00:30:54.588
I know who to call.


00:31:09.336 --> 00:31:12.105
No! Please, please! No, no!


00:31:13.440 --> 00:31:15.174
This year, man. What's next?


00:31:15.209 --> 00:31:18.645
Historically, uh, darkness,
blood, rain of fire.


00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:20.213
I think frogs.


00:31:20.247 --> 00:31:22.025
We're not gonna be around
for much longer anyway.


00:31:22.048 --> 00:31:23.560
These locusts in Nebraska
are about to wrap it up.


00:31:23.585 --> 00:31:25.152
They're eating the corn, wheat.


00:31:25.184 --> 00:31:27.121
Basically all of our food
and our food's food.


00:31:27.153 --> 00:31:29.523
So we can say goodbye to this.


00:31:32.326 --> 00:31:34.528
- Hello?
- Franklin, it's me.


00:31:34.561 --> 00:31:35.996
- You at work?
- Okay.


00:31:36.028 --> 00:31:37.998
You're kind of a subject
of interest around here,


00:31:38.030 --> 00:31:39.601
so I can't really
be talking to you.


00:31:39.634 --> 00:31:40.933
Come on, I'm in trouble.


00:31:40.968 --> 00:31:42.211
I really need your help, please.


00:31:42.236 --> 00:31:44.003
Yeah, and I could lose my job,


00:31:44.037 --> 00:31:45.548
and you know I'm not qualified
to do anything else.


00:31:45.573 --> 00:31:47.039
We're outside.


00:31:49.242 --> 00:31:51.010
Let me talk to him.


00:31:54.414 --> 00:31:55.415
That him?


00:31:55.449 --> 00:31:56.683
That's him.


00:31:56.718 --> 00:31:59.019
Name's Rainn Delacourt.


00:31:59.051 --> 00:32:00.587
Real piece of work.


00:32:00.622 --> 00:32:02.189
What'd he take?


00:32:03.056 --> 00:32:05.358
Something we care about
very much.


00:32:05.392 --> 00:32:07.126
Oh, shit.


00:32:07.161 --> 00:32:09.028
I told you somebody
would come looking for her.


00:32:09.061 --> 00:32:10.731
You can't just take
a person, Claire.


00:32:10.765 --> 00:32:13.133
- I had no choice.
- Not in the eyes of the law.


00:32:13.166 --> 00:32:16.135
This guy is not the law.
Tell us how to find him.


00:32:17.538 --> 00:32:19.373
Where'd you guys call me from?


00:32:20.374 --> 00:32:23.477
We have a man on the inside
of Delacourt's operation.


00:32:23.510 --> 00:32:24.711
There's an exchange in Malta


00:32:24.746 --> 00:32:26.313
sometime tomorrow...
cash for cargo.


00:32:26.346 --> 00:32:27.615
Was she with him?


00:32:28.916 --> 00:32:31.752
There's no mention, but we have
people on the ground already.


00:32:31.786 --> 00:32:33.186
One of 'em you know.


00:32:33.220 --> 00:32:34.597
A lot of us got recruited
by the CIA


00:32:34.622 --> 00:32:36.190
after the park went down.


00:32:37.625 --> 00:32:39.358
Barry's French intelligence now.


00:32:41.494 --> 00:32:42.596
I need to talk to him.


00:32:42.630 --> 00:32:44.598
You can't just call him.
He's deep cover.


00:32:44.632 --> 00:32:46.365
Look, once we make
the bust in Malta,


00:32:46.400 --> 00:32:48.736
our guys will see if Delacourt
knows where she is.


00:32:48.769 --> 00:32:50.605
Our guys.


00:32:50.637 --> 00:32:52.072
Not you.


00:32:52.105 --> 00:32:55.075
Promise me you won't go in there
with your vest


00:32:55.107 --> 00:32:56.977
and mess everything up.


00:32:57.612 --> 00:32:59.112
Why would I do that?


00:33:00.113 --> 00:33:03.317
Look, you guys
are both crazy, but...


00:33:03.349 --> 00:33:05.117
you seem like
you're good parents


00:33:05.152 --> 00:33:06.788
or whatever you're trying to be.


00:33:06.820 --> 00:33:09.222
She's lucky to have you.


00:33:10.457 --> 00:33:13.059
Don't get killed, okay?


00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:32.680
Think we're almost there.


00:33:32.713 --> 00:33:34.280
Yeah.


00:33:47.662 --> 00:33:49.429
Dr. Sattler, Dr. Grant.


00:33:49.462 --> 00:33:51.464
- Ramsay Cole, communications.
- Oh, hey.


00:33:51.498 --> 00:33:52.700
Uh, I have to warn you,


00:33:52.733 --> 00:33:54.300
everyone's so excited
to have you.


00:33:54.334 --> 00:33:56.570
You guys are absolute legends
around here.


00:33:56.604 --> 00:33:59.405
Mm, you must be confusing us
with somebody else.


00:33:59.439 --> 00:34:00.508
You know, it's great


00:34:00.541 --> 00:34:02.644
that you guys are still
so close with Dr. Malcolm.


00:34:02.676 --> 00:34:05.579
I mean, sometimes you meet your
heroes and they disappoint you,


00:34:05.613 --> 00:34:08.081
but he's exactly the way
you'd want him to be.


00:34:08.114 --> 00:34:09.324
I mean,
such motility of thought.


00:34:09.349 --> 00:34:10.684
- It's incredible.
- Yeah.


00:34:10.717 --> 00:34:12.351
How much time
have you spent with him?


00:34:12.385 --> 00:34:15.121
Uh, well,
I know that was sarcastic,


00:34:15.155 --> 00:34:16.489
but honestly, not enough.


00:34:16.523 --> 00:34:17.592
Oh, please, after you.


00:34:17.625 --> 00:34:18.826
- Oh.
- And watch your head.


00:34:25.867 --> 00:34:28.201
So, Biosyn bought this
land for the amber deposits


00:34:28.235 --> 00:34:30.170
back in the '90s,
but we've managed to turn it


00:34:30.202 --> 00:34:32.507
into a safe haven
for about 20 displaced species.


00:34:32.539 --> 00:34:34.509
First generation came
from Sorna.


00:34:34.541 --> 00:34:36.510
Most of the Nublar dinosaurs
are here, too.


00:34:36.543 --> 00:34:39.614
Took Fish and Wildlife
three years to catch the T. rex.


00:34:39.646 --> 00:34:42.181
- The...
- The T. rex is here?


00:34:42.215 --> 00:34:44.552
Oh, yeah. Yeah.


00:34:44.585 --> 00:34:47.621
Arrived just before you guys.


00:35:04.271 --> 00:35:07.206
Aerial deterrent system active.


00:35:07.239 --> 00:35:10.210
Restricted airspace
protects the airborne life.


00:35:10.242 --> 00:35:12.547
Keeps the pterosaurs
below 500 feet.


00:35:12.579 --> 00:35:14.114
Airborne?


00:35:15.682 --> 00:35:17.751
Is that <i>Dreadnoughtus?</i>


00:35:17.784 --> 00:35:19.519
What?


00:35:26.661 --> 00:35:28.327
Beautiful, right?


00:35:28.362 --> 00:35:30.364
The name means "fear nothing."


00:35:30.396 --> 00:35:32.766
Well, I guess you know that.


00:35:32.800 --> 00:35:33.934
What do they graze on?


00:35:33.967 --> 00:35:35.302
Hawthorn and fern.


00:35:35.335 --> 00:35:36.871
All indigenous... nothing stocked


00:35:36.903 --> 00:35:38.606
except for the deer population.


00:35:38.639 --> 00:35:41.909
It's a great mezzanine species
for the apex predator.


00:35:41.943 --> 00:35:43.911
- Oh...
- Apex predator?


00:35:43.945 --> 00:35:46.547
<i>Giganotosaurus.</i>


00:35:46.581 --> 00:35:48.650
At least for now.


00:35:57.958 --> 00:36:00.961
Uh, you don't let people
in there, right?


00:36:00.994 --> 00:36:03.396
Uh, no, our-our research...


00:36:03.429 --> 00:36:05.297
Our research outposts
are connected


00:36:05.331 --> 00:36:06.400
completely underground.


00:36:06.432 --> 00:36:07.934
If we have to, we can just


00:36:07.969 --> 00:36:11.271
herd the animals remotely
using a neuro-implant


00:36:11.304 --> 00:36:13.541
that sends electrical signals
directly to the brain.


00:36:13.574 --> 00:36:14.909
Like shocks?


00:36:14.942 --> 00:36:17.744
Uh, n-no, li-like signals.


00:36:17.778 --> 00:36:20.882
Doesn't it strike you
as a little bit, uh...


00:36:20.914 --> 00:36:22.416
- Cruel?
- Cruel.


00:36:22.449 --> 00:36:23.951
Do you know how much voltage


00:36:23.985 --> 00:36:26.721
was in the electric fences
at Jurassic Park?


00:36:27.655 --> 00:36:28.655
Yeah.


00:36:34.594 --> 00:36:36.597
Please join
Dr. Ian Malcolm at noon


00:36:36.630 --> 00:36:39.634
in the lecture hall for
"The Ethics of Genetic Power."


00:36:39.666 --> 00:36:41.434
God, everyone's so young.


00:36:41.467 --> 00:36:43.235
Oh, well, it is part
of our ethos


00:36:43.269 --> 00:36:44.938
to attract the best
and brightest.


00:36:44.972 --> 00:36:46.708
Doctors.


00:36:46.740 --> 00:36:50.811
Respected, renowned
Dr. Sattler, Dr. Grant.


00:36:50.844 --> 00:36:52.947
Hi. I'm... Wow, this is big.


00:36:52.980 --> 00:36:55.347
- I'm-I'm Lewis.
- Dodgson. Yeah.


00:36:55.382 --> 00:36:56.751
- Hi.
- You're Lewis Dodgson?


00:36:56.784 --> 00:36:58.018
I am. How do you do?


00:36:58.052 --> 00:37:00.320
We didn't expect
to actually see you here.


00:37:00.353 --> 00:37:01.498
Oh, well, I wouldn't be
anywhere else.


00:37:01.521 --> 00:37:03.724
- Would you?
- No.


00:37:03.757 --> 00:37:06.460
I mean, the people you see here
are changing the world.


00:37:06.492 --> 00:37:07.862
Would you mind if we, um...


00:37:07.894 --> 00:37:09.597
- Uh...
- Oh.


00:37:09.630 --> 00:37:11.599
Just to...
It would mean a lot. If...


00:37:11.632 --> 00:37:13.034
Do you want to, um...


00:37:13.067 --> 00:37:14.802
- Oh, great. Thank you so much.
- Oh, uh...


00:37:16.070 --> 00:37:17.739
Th-That's good.
That's good. Thanks.


00:37:17.771 --> 00:37:22.442
So, you are going to see
some remarkable things today.


00:37:22.476 --> 00:37:25.980
We are unlocking
the true power of the genome.


00:37:26.012 --> 00:37:27.748
We're this close. Believe me.


00:37:27.782 --> 00:37:29.684
You'll make a fortune with that.


00:37:29.717 --> 00:37:31.753
No, it's not about money.


00:37:31.786 --> 00:37:33.353
No, we've already identified


00:37:33.385 --> 00:37:34.797
dozens of applications
for paleo-DNA.


00:37:34.822 --> 00:37:38.793
We're talking about cancer,
Alzheimer's, autoimmune.


00:37:38.826 --> 00:37:40.561
We will be saving lives, but...


00:37:40.594 --> 00:37:42.362
I bet.


00:37:42.394 --> 00:37:44.766
Um, anyway, I wish I could
take you around myself,


00:37:44.798 --> 00:37:46.500
but, uh, it's, uh...


00:37:46.534 --> 00:37:49.804
So, you're in more-than-capable
hands with Ramsay.


00:37:49.836 --> 00:37:52.907
He's basically a... a young me,


00:37:52.940 --> 00:37:56.476
only smarter and, uh, taller...


00:37:56.510 --> 00:37:59.378
Do you have food?


00:37:59.411 --> 00:38:01.681
- Like, one of my bars?
- Pardon? Um...


00:38:01.715 --> 00:38:04.085
No, never mind.
Uh, uh, I'll find something.


00:38:04.117 --> 00:38:06.318
So, uh, I want to do
more of this,


00:38:06.353 --> 00:38:08.454
um, later on if we, um...


00:38:08.487 --> 00:38:10.489
Oh, we booked you a private pod


00:38:10.525 --> 00:38:12.324
- for the trip out, so...
- Right.


00:38:12.358 --> 00:38:13.570
It's beautiful. You'll love it.


00:38:13.594 --> 00:38:15.061
Through the caverns
and everything.


00:38:15.096 --> 00:38:16.597
Uh, you better hurry.
Malcolm's on.


00:38:16.630 --> 00:38:18.900
He's a bit of a contrarian,
but I like him.


00:38:18.932 --> 00:38:20.333
He keeps us on our toes.


00:38:20.367 --> 00:38:21.536
Anyway...


00:38:21.568 --> 00:38:23.704
Thank you for being here.
It's...


00:38:25.940 --> 00:38:28.576
Okay, um, follow me, please.


00:38:30.077 --> 00:38:31.679
What?


00:38:31.711 --> 00:38:37.083
Human beings have no more right
to safety or liberty


00:38:37.117 --> 00:38:40.554
than any other creature
on this planet.


00:38:41.989 --> 00:38:46.827
We not only lack dominion
over nature,


00:38:46.860 --> 00:38:48.862
we're subordinate to it.


00:38:49.864 --> 00:38:51.565
And now here we are


00:38:51.599 --> 00:38:54.869
with the opportunity to
rewrite life at our fingertips.


00:38:54.902 --> 00:38:57.972
And just like nuclear power,
nobody knew what to expect


00:38:58.005 --> 00:39:01.775
with genetic engineering,
but they pressed the button


00:39:01.809 --> 00:39:04.644
and hoped for the best...


00:39:04.679 --> 00:39:07.581
just like you are doing now.


00:39:08.615 --> 00:39:10.784
Yep. You.


00:39:11.918 --> 00:39:17.489
You control the future
of our survival on planet Earth.


00:39:17.525 --> 00:39:20.460
According to you,
the solution is genetic power.


00:39:20.492 --> 00:39:23.864
But that same power could
devastate the food supply,


00:39:23.898 --> 00:39:26.132
create new diseases,


00:39:26.166 --> 00:39:28.501
alter the climate even further.


00:39:28.536 --> 00:39:32.438
Unforeseen consequences occur.


00:39:32.472 --> 00:39:37.777
And every time,
every single time...


00:39:39.213 --> 00:39:41.481
...we all act surprised?


00:39:41.514 --> 00:39:44.451
Because deep down,
I don't think that any of us


00:39:44.483 --> 00:39:47.655
actually believe
that these dangers are real.


00:39:54.929 --> 00:39:58.632
In order to instigate
revolutionary change,


00:39:58.666 --> 00:40:04.771
we must transform
human consciousness.


00:40:12.112 --> 00:40:13.547
- Mayam?
- Mm-hmm.


00:40:13.581 --> 00:40:15.215
- Dr. Malcolm?
- Very good.


00:40:15.248 --> 00:40:16.851
There-there you go.


00:40:16.884 --> 00:40:18.896
Hey, I don't want to be rude
to my friends. Thank you.


00:40:18.920 --> 00:40:21.188
Catch me on my way out.
Thanks, everybody.


00:40:21.222 --> 00:40:22.657
Look at you,


00:40:22.690 --> 00:40:26.594
and look at me, and look at you.


00:40:26.626 --> 00:40:28.460
Wow, this is so trippy.


00:40:28.494 --> 00:40:30.563
You look like you're doing well.


00:40:30.597 --> 00:40:31.932
Well, I got five kids, you know,


00:40:31.965 --> 00:40:34.068
whom I adore
more than life itself, so...


00:40:34.101 --> 00:40:35.635
uh, expenses add up.


00:40:35.670 --> 00:40:38.072
You, Alan? Are you... are you...


00:40:38.105 --> 00:40:40.141
You have any family or...?


00:40:40.173 --> 00:40:41.175
No.


00:40:41.208 --> 00:40:43.643
So, uh, I need to talk to you.


00:40:43.677 --> 00:40:45.211
Yeah, I need to talk
to you, too.


00:40:45.246 --> 00:40:47.715
- Privately.
- Do you two talk a lot?


00:40:47.748 --> 00:40:49.849
- Uh, he slid into my DMs.
- He did what?


00:40:49.884 --> 00:40:52.152
- It's urgent, Ian.
- What did you do?


00:40:52.186 --> 00:40:53.853
"Seven minutes to midnight"
stuff.


00:40:53.887 --> 00:40:56.257
Uh, the Doomsday Clock
might be about out of time,


00:40:56.289 --> 00:40:59.092
but as they say,
it's always darkest


00:40:59.126 --> 00:41:01.896
just before eternal nothingness.


00:41:01.929 --> 00:41:03.563
What?


00:41:05.099 --> 00:41:08.568
Locusts,
altered with Cretaceous-era DNA.


00:41:08.601 --> 00:41:09.903
Yeah, that's not my field.


00:41:09.936 --> 00:41:11.938
Yeah, but if these things
continue to multiply,


00:41:11.972 --> 00:41:14.976
we're talking about cascading
system-wide effects, Ian.


00:41:15.009 --> 00:41:16.610
Gosh, that's a drag.


00:41:16.643 --> 00:41:18.679
What is the matter with you?


00:41:18.713 --> 00:41:20.657
Why? Is there something special
you want me to do?


00:41:20.681 --> 00:41:21.849
Yeah, how about give a damn?


00:41:21.882 --> 00:41:23.550
You know far too much
not to care.


00:41:23.583 --> 00:41:26.987
Hey, I-I gave my opinion
robustly for years.


00:41:27.021 --> 00:41:28.989
As expected,
the sum of our human endeavors


00:41:29.023 --> 00:41:32.259
has led to our annihilation,
and the only play now


00:41:32.293 --> 00:41:34.929
is to take the time
that we have left and, uh,


00:41:34.961 --> 00:41:37.264
you know, just like
we always do, squander it.


00:41:37.297 --> 00:41:40.534
Honestly, Ian, that's bullshit.


00:41:40.568 --> 00:41:42.702
Can I offer you guys some joe?


00:41:42.737 --> 00:41:46.606
Uh, Tyler, please,
two cappuccinos.


00:41:46.639 --> 00:41:48.108
I don't want a cappuccino.


00:41:48.141 --> 00:41:49.920
Uh, well, I could do, like,
a cortado or, like, macchiato.


00:41:49.943 --> 00:41:52.012
Trust me, it's real tough,
that jet lag.


00:41:52.045 --> 00:41:53.206
It's gonna perk you right up.


00:41:57.184 --> 00:41:59.320
The locusts are part
of a larger project


00:41:59.353 --> 00:42:01.155
called Hexapod Allies.


00:42:01.188 --> 00:42:02.690
You're right about their intent.


00:42:02.722 --> 00:42:04.958
I started hearing rumors
six weeks ago.


00:42:04.992 --> 00:42:07.304
I read your piece on decadence
and put two and two together.


00:42:07.327 --> 00:42:08.929
I was not raising my voice.


00:42:08.963 --> 00:42:10.639
You're beginning to.
It's crescendoing, isn't it?


00:42:10.664 --> 00:42:12.166
They're proliferating wildly.


00:42:12.199 --> 00:42:14.344
They're lasting three, four
times longer than they should.


00:42:14.367 --> 00:42:16.704
And all my models
are pointing toward a global


00:42:16.737 --> 00:42:18.271
ecological collapse, Ian.


00:42:18.304 --> 00:42:19.907
Downstairs, sublevel six.


00:42:19.940 --> 00:42:22.043
That's where they keep
the locusts.


00:42:22.076 --> 00:42:23.943
Look for a lab marked L4.


00:42:23.978 --> 00:42:25.846
But wait, how are we ever
gonna get down there?


00:42:25.880 --> 00:42:27.648
Hey, this looks so silky.


00:42:27.681 --> 00:42:29.282
May I touch this blouse,
by any chance?


00:42:29.315 --> 00:42:30.918
- Sure.
- You know what it is?


00:42:30.951 --> 00:42:32.728
- Don't tell... Don't tell me.
- You won't know it.


00:42:32.753 --> 00:42:34.755
This is sustainable bamboo.


00:42:34.789 --> 00:42:36.733
- It is sustainable bamboo.
- That's why I said it.


00:42:36.757 --> 00:42:38.135
- How did you know that?
- I just know it.


00:42:38.159 --> 00:42:39.793
- Yeah, it's amazing.
- I've got cumin.


00:42:39.827 --> 00:42:41.137
- It's very amazing.
- I've got cinnamon.


00:42:41.161 --> 00:42:42.838
I've got allspice,
which is not very popular.


00:42:42.862 --> 00:42:44.331
- I've got five-spice.
- Doctor.


00:42:44.364 --> 00:42:45.675
Um, if you're into
that kind of feel.


00:42:45.699 --> 00:42:48.601
- Um, and let's talk milks.
- Yeah.


00:42:48.635 --> 00:42:50.670
Okay. Soy milk, yes?


00:42:52.005 --> 00:42:54.608
- No.
- What just happened?


00:42:54.641 --> 00:42:56.577
We're in.


00:43:09.789 --> 00:43:12.860
Sublevel six. Restricted.


00:43:18.731 --> 00:43:21.335
Lewis,
you're not listening to me.


00:43:21.367 --> 00:43:23.336
The locusts' prehistoric DNA
has made them


00:43:23.369 --> 00:43:25.106
stronger than they should be.


00:43:25.139 --> 00:43:27.875
They're multiplying like crazy,
and they're not dying.


00:43:27.907 --> 00:43:29.385
What part of this
don't you understand?


00:43:29.409 --> 00:43:30.777
Oh, I do understand.


00:43:30.811 --> 00:43:32.679
This is gonna be
a global famine.


00:43:32.713 --> 00:43:34.380
Hey, hey, we can't
anticipate everything.


00:43:34.414 --> 00:43:37.117
We need to eradicate
the ones we released.


00:43:37.150 --> 00:43:38.853
- What?
- All of them.


00:43:38.885 --> 00:43:41.155
- No. No. Henry.
- Like... like, yesterday.


00:43:41.188 --> 00:43:42.922
We don't want to cause a panic.


00:43:42.956 --> 00:43:44.391
We want control.


00:43:44.425 --> 00:43:46.893
There is no such thing.


00:43:58.938 --> 00:44:02.275
When we're afraid,
what do we do?


00:44:02.309 --> 00:44:04.244
What have we done before?


00:44:04.277 --> 00:44:07.148
We follow through.


00:44:07.181 --> 00:44:09.083
That's what we do.


00:44:09.115 --> 00:44:10.784
Right?


00:44:12.920 --> 00:44:14.255
Right.


00:44:17.056 --> 00:44:18.425
We found the girl.


00:44:18.458 --> 00:44:20.161
She's en route.


00:44:20.193 --> 00:44:22.228
- Cost me a fortune.
- What?


00:44:22.262 --> 00:44:24.864
- Wait, you found her?
- Yeah, found them both.


00:44:24.898 --> 00:44:27.300
Her and the little raptor.


00:44:27.333 --> 00:44:29.869
Blue reproduced all on her own.


00:44:30.838 --> 00:44:33.007
Just like you said.
You're so smart, Henry.


00:44:35.208 --> 00:44:37.443
That's why this works.


00:44:37.478 --> 00:44:39.780
You understand the value
of these creatures.


00:44:39.813 --> 00:44:41.315
You always have. I do, too.


00:44:41.347 --> 00:44:43.751
And we don't stop
because a, what,


00:44:43.784 --> 00:44:45.686
little side project went south?


00:44:47.054 --> 00:44:50.757
Hey. If they trace
the locusts back to us,


00:44:50.791 --> 00:44:52.293
they come for the dinosaurs.


00:44:52.326 --> 00:44:54.027
All your work gone.


00:44:54.994 --> 00:44:58.032
Billions of dollars
in assets gone.


00:44:59.132 --> 00:45:02.135
Diamonds with no one
to mine them.


00:45:03.036 --> 00:45:05.271
You really think
she's the solution?


00:45:08.409 --> 00:45:10.344
Okay.


00:45:11.378 --> 00:45:14.014
Everything involving the girl
goes through me, right?


00:45:15.882 --> 00:45:17.384
Is she all right?


00:45:17.418 --> 00:45:18.952
She better be.


00:45:19.554 --> 00:45:21.054
She's the most valuable


00:45:21.088 --> 00:45:23.257
intellectual property
on the planet.


00:45:33.266 --> 00:45:34.835
I said I'd call you.


00:45:34.867 --> 00:45:36.103
They land yet?


00:45:36.135 --> 00:45:37.838
Second plane is incoming.


00:45:37.871 --> 00:45:39.248
Who said anything
about a second plane?


00:45:39.273 --> 00:45:40.541
We flew them separately.


00:45:40.574 --> 00:45:42.009
I'm not taking any chances.


00:45:42.041 --> 00:45:44.411
And we'll need payment
before delivery.


00:45:44.445 --> 00:45:46.514
I didn't like
what happened last time.


00:45:46.547 --> 00:45:50.117
Okay. Okay, just...
call me when it's done.


00:45:59.460 --> 00:46:01.829
You said I was going
someplace safe.


00:46:02.463 --> 00:46:03.565
You are.


00:46:10.903 --> 00:46:12.373
Walk to the car.


00:46:13.373 --> 00:46:16.043
- No.
- It's not a choice.


00:46:28.956 --> 00:46:32.226
50 grand to fly
one little raptor.


00:46:32.259 --> 00:46:34.193
Not bad.


00:46:38.965 --> 00:46:40.367
What's with the girl?


00:46:42.902 --> 00:46:45.204
Not your problem.


00:46:52.945 --> 00:46:55.416
Pleasure doing business.


00:46:58.351 --> 00:47:00.320
We're ready. Let's go.


00:47:06.360 --> 00:47:07.960
Owen.


00:47:13.032 --> 00:47:14.967
- Hi, Claire.
- Mm.


00:47:15.001 --> 00:47:17.605
I thought you would've chosen
a quieter line of work.


00:47:17.639 --> 00:47:19.472
I tried.
My cousin and I opened a café.


00:47:19.507 --> 00:47:21.307
I lasted three weeks.


00:47:21.342 --> 00:47:24.077
The way the world is headed,
it's hard to look away.


00:47:24.110 --> 00:47:27.047
<i>Delacourt was hired
by Soyona Santos,</i>


00:47:27.081 --> 00:47:29.083
a broker in
the underground dinosaur trade.


00:47:29.115 --> 00:47:31.385
We don't have intel
on his cargo,


00:47:31.418 --> 00:47:33.219
but once they make the exchange,


00:47:33.253 --> 00:47:35.222
we'll see what they know
about your girl.


00:47:35.255 --> 00:47:36.190
You can listen in,


00:47:36.222 --> 00:47:38.391
but promise me
you will not make contact.


00:47:38.425 --> 00:47:39.992
No.


00:47:41.994 --> 00:47:43.230
<i>Ouais, c'est ça.</i>


00:47:43.262 --> 00:47:44.965
<i>There is a big
underground market</i>


00:47:44.998 --> 00:47:46.233
<i>for dinosaurs now...</i>


00:47:46.266 --> 00:47:48.469
<i>Europe, Middle East,
northern Africa.</i>


00:47:48.501 --> 00:47:50.237
It all comes through here.


00:48:00.481 --> 00:48:03.384
Don't look at anyone.
Don't talk to anyone.


00:48:03.416 --> 00:48:05.251
Just try to blend in.


00:48:54.536 --> 00:48:57.170
Hey, still flying
for Santos, huh?


00:48:57.204 --> 00:48:59.507
- You must need money.
- What's it to you?


00:48:59.541 --> 00:49:01.442
I've got cargo.


00:49:01.474 --> 00:49:04.445
Thousand kilos of dinosaur
to Palermo.


00:49:04.478 --> 00:49:06.681
I give you 2,000.


00:49:06.713 --> 00:49:09.349
2,000? How much is there?


00:49:18.760 --> 00:49:20.628
You lost?


00:49:20.661 --> 00:49:22.329
You're American.


00:49:23.630 --> 00:49:25.097
That make us friends?


00:49:25.132 --> 00:49:27.201
Listen, I just got here, and...


00:49:27.233 --> 00:49:30.403
Oh, no, that was not
an invitation. Here.


00:49:32.639 --> 00:49:34.509
Souvenir. Go back to the hotel.


00:49:34.541 --> 00:49:37.077
You know, throw some bath salts
in the bath.


00:49:37.110 --> 00:49:39.581
This place... not your vibe.


00:49:39.614 --> 00:49:41.583
Wait.


00:49:41.615 --> 00:49:43.518
- Look...
- Claire.


00:49:44.384 --> 00:49:47.186
Claire, I know this must
feel exotic,


00:49:47.221 --> 00:49:49.489
but if you mess with
the wrong person down here,


00:49:49.523 --> 00:49:50.592
you disappear.


00:49:50.625 --> 00:49:51.693
You feel me?


00:49:51.726 --> 00:49:55.027
- Good luck, okay?
- Wait.


00:49:57.532 --> 00:49:59.199
- Wait.
- What is this?


00:49:59.233 --> 00:50:01.268
- I need your help.
- I don't know you.


00:50:01.300 --> 00:50:03.436
- I'm looking for someone.
- Don't do that.


00:50:03.469 --> 00:50:05.572
She is all alone. Please.


00:50:11.143 --> 00:50:14.014
- That your daughter?
- Yes.


00:50:16.315 --> 00:50:18.418
Sorry. I can't get involved.


00:50:36.871 --> 00:50:38.472
Think I got him.


00:50:38.505 --> 00:50:39.673
Target on the move.


00:50:40.574 --> 00:50:42.777
That's our undercover agent
with him.


00:50:42.809 --> 00:50:44.778
Claire, he's headed underground.


00:50:44.811 --> 00:50:46.445
- See him?
- Yeah, I've got him.


00:50:48.516 --> 00:50:49.684
All right, let's go.


00:50:49.717 --> 00:50:51.150
<i>Team four,</i>


00:50:51.184 --> 00:50:52.503
<i>need you to sweep
spreading south.</i>


00:50:56.456 --> 00:50:59.059
All units,
take up bull's-eye position.


00:51:00.193 --> 00:51:02.697
This is Bravo One.
Primary target in sight.


00:51:02.730 --> 00:51:04.431
No sign of the girl.


00:51:04.463 --> 00:51:06.166
Alpha team, stand clear.


00:51:16.342 --> 00:51:20.614
My people say the raptor
arrived in good condition.


00:51:20.648 --> 00:51:22.717
You boys didn't cock this up.


00:51:22.750 --> 00:51:24.585
Color me amazed.


00:51:24.619 --> 00:51:26.219
I do have another job for you.


00:51:26.253 --> 00:51:27.855
Short hop. Money's double.


00:51:27.889 --> 00:51:29.456
What's the cargo?


00:51:31.224 --> 00:51:33.561
<i>Atrociraptors.</i>


00:51:33.594 --> 00:51:35.128
Thoroughbreds.


00:51:35.161 --> 00:51:36.530
Trained to kill.


00:51:36.563 --> 00:51:37.632
Kill who?


00:51:37.664 --> 00:51:39.333
Whoever they're told.


00:51:39.365 --> 00:51:41.210
Laser marks the target,
they attach to the scent,


00:51:41.233 --> 00:51:42.603
don't stop till it's dead.


00:51:42.637 --> 00:51:43.871
Inescapable.


00:51:43.905 --> 00:51:46.239
Those idiots making hybrids
had it all wrong.


00:51:46.273 --> 00:51:48.342
You can't engineer loyalty.


00:51:48.375 --> 00:51:50.210
You have to nurture it.


00:51:50.242 --> 00:51:52.579
50,000 to fly them to Riyadh.


00:51:52.614 --> 00:51:54.681
In or out?


00:51:54.715 --> 00:51:56.684
She's not here.


00:52:00.588 --> 00:52:02.389
Where are we going?


00:52:03.255 --> 00:52:04.626
Almost there.


00:52:10.429 --> 00:52:11.898
That's the drop. Let's go.


00:52:11.932 --> 00:52:14.233
- Weapons down!
- Eyes on 'em!


00:52:14.266 --> 00:52:15.737
- Hands in the air!
- Contact made!


00:52:15.769 --> 00:52:18.237
Delacourt, on the floor now!


00:52:18.271 --> 00:52:19.338
Get on the ground!


00:52:19.373 --> 00:52:20.942
Delacourt! Stay with him!


00:52:20.974 --> 00:52:22.476
Shit.


00:52:23.878 --> 00:52:25.378
Get that truck out of here!


00:52:33.286 --> 00:52:34.789
We lost Delacourt!


00:52:46.867 --> 00:52:48.536
This is Bravo One.


00:52:48.568 --> 00:52:50.505
Truck is approaching
the underpass.


00:54:04.376 --> 00:54:06.012
Come on!


00:54:20.927 --> 00:54:22.329
The girl, where is she?


00:54:22.362 --> 00:54:24.030
- Where did they take her?
- Get it off!


00:54:24.065 --> 00:54:25.900
- Where is she?
- I don't know!


00:54:25.932 --> 00:54:27.702
We handed her off to Santos.


00:54:27.735 --> 00:54:30.003
I don't know where
they took her after that.


00:54:42.949 --> 00:54:44.684
Claire, it's Santos.


00:54:44.719 --> 00:54:46.586
- The woman in white.
- I'll find her.


00:54:46.621 --> 00:54:49.422
Bravo team, watch your six.


00:54:50.389 --> 00:54:52.659
Hey, hey!


00:54:52.693 --> 00:54:54.594
- Hey!
- Hold it!


00:54:54.628 --> 00:54:56.496
Let them out.


00:54:56.530 --> 00:54:57.329
What?!


00:54:57.364 --> 00:54:59.465
You heard me.


00:55:23.990 --> 00:55:25.827
Merde.


00:55:43.476 --> 00:55:45.512
Claire, do you have her?


00:55:58.893 --> 00:56:00.393
We had some trouble.


00:56:00.427 --> 00:56:02.128
- What kind?
- The parents.


00:56:02.163 --> 00:56:04.164
Grady and Dearing...
they're here.


00:56:08.135 --> 00:56:09.737
Can you take care of it?


00:56:09.769 --> 00:56:11.438
Not for free.


00:56:11.471 --> 00:56:13.608
Well, do it.


00:56:21.481 --> 00:56:24.416
Mama.


00:56:28.054 --> 00:56:29.856
Okay, okay, listen.


00:56:29.891 --> 00:56:31.490
No, no, no.


00:56:44.572 --> 00:56:46.507
You don't use it on people.


00:56:46.539 --> 00:56:47.641
Where's my daughter?


00:56:47.675 --> 00:56:50.043
She wasn't yours to begin with.


00:56:52.045 --> 00:56:53.914
Tell me.


00:56:55.115 --> 00:56:56.650
Biosyn.


00:56:56.684 --> 00:56:59.820
They're taking her to Biosyn.


00:57:05.092 --> 00:57:07.128
You missed her.


00:57:07.161 --> 00:57:08.728
She's gone.


00:58:00.581 --> 00:58:02.148
Take my hand. Come on.


00:58:32.947 --> 00:58:34.280
Hold on tight.


00:58:34.315 --> 00:58:36.083
What?


00:58:46.226 --> 00:58:49.130
Do you remember how we used to
get the raptors in the truck?


00:58:49.163 --> 00:58:50.797
- Yeah.
- Yeah.


00:58:52.065 --> 00:58:53.333
- You're up.
- No.


00:58:55.302 --> 00:58:56.637
At the last minute, dive-roll.


00:58:56.670 --> 00:58:58.806
- I don't dive-roll.
- You'll be fine.


00:58:58.838 --> 00:59:01.007
I never got the timing right.


00:59:02.342 --> 00:59:03.677
Now?


00:59:03.710 --> 00:59:05.679
Any minute. Any minute now.


00:59:06.280 --> 00:59:08.081
- Now?
- No.


00:59:10.217 --> 00:59:11.751
Now!


00:59:14.655 --> 00:59:17.123
Yeah. Yeah!


00:59:18.224 --> 00:59:19.592
Freeze.


00:59:26.800 --> 00:59:28.001
I'm flying us out of here.


00:59:28.034 --> 00:59:29.702
Tell me where
you want to be dropped.


00:59:29.737 --> 00:59:31.172
You ever flown to Biosyn?


00:59:32.739 --> 00:59:34.942
Owen, they took her to Biosyn!


00:59:34.974 --> 00:59:37.311
There's an airfield on the
north side of the island. -Go.


00:59:37.344 --> 00:59:39.012
You're under arrest.


00:59:39.045 --> 00:59:40.748
Stay where you are.


01:00:06.873 --> 01:00:08.775
Right!


01:00:13.246 --> 01:00:14.347
Heads up!


01:01:52.313 --> 01:01:54.014
We made a lot of enemies today.


01:01:54.047 --> 01:01:54.949
We got to go.


01:01:54.981 --> 01:01:56.518
- He'll be here.
- Uh-huh.


01:02:00.387 --> 01:02:02.789
Out of time, out of time.


01:02:04.257 --> 01:02:06.025
There he is.


01:02:07.927 --> 01:02:10.331
- Pull over.
- That's not how planes work.


01:02:16.538 --> 01:02:18.304
Open the back.


01:02:36.990 --> 01:02:38.157
Come on!


01:02:42.896 --> 01:02:45.898
Hold on tight!


01:03:01.849 --> 01:03:04.318
Oh, sh...


01:03:14.862 --> 01:03:16.329
Still got it.


01:03:35.349 --> 01:03:37.483
Kayla Watts.


01:03:37.518 --> 01:03:39.219
You're welcome.


01:03:39.253 --> 01:03:41.221
You don't look like
you fly for Biosyn.


01:03:41.255 --> 01:03:42.889
I'm gonna take that
the way you meant it


01:03:42.922 --> 01:03:44.858
and not the way it sounded.


01:03:44.891 --> 01:03:46.360
I fly from whoever got a bag,


01:03:46.393 --> 01:03:47.960
but we'll call this one a favor.


01:03:47.994 --> 01:03:50.864
Those don't work. They broke.


01:03:51.998 --> 01:03:53.300
I'll take y'all to Biosyn,


01:03:53.333 --> 01:03:55.302
but I can't promise
it won't be dangerous.


01:03:55.335 --> 01:03:58.371
You're willing to risk your
life for people you never met?


01:03:59.641 --> 01:04:02.976
You want to ask questions,
or you want a ride?


01:04:05.612 --> 01:04:07.347
We'll take the ride.


01:04:14.288 --> 01:04:16.389
So, this is our habitat
development lab.


01:04:16.422 --> 01:04:19.092
A lot of exciting discoveries
as of late.


01:04:19.126 --> 01:04:20.594
We've brought back
numerous species


01:04:20.628 --> 01:04:22.028
in their purest form,


01:04:22.061 --> 01:04:24.364
and I mean complete,
untouched genomes.


01:04:24.398 --> 01:04:25.998
Like <i>Moros intrepidus.</i>


01:04:26.032 --> 01:04:27.635
- What?
- Yeah.


01:04:29.202 --> 01:04:30.572
Wow.


01:04:33.641 --> 01:04:35.543
What about splicing DNA?


01:04:35.577 --> 01:04:37.378
You know, creating new species?


01:04:37.411 --> 01:04:40.047
Uh, no, Dr. Sattler,
we don't do that here.


01:04:40.079 --> 01:04:42.148
We like to think
we're more evolved.


01:04:46.721 --> 01:04:48.021
Okay, it looks like
we still have


01:04:48.054 --> 01:04:49.099
some time left before your ride.


01:04:49.123 --> 01:04:51.157
Uh, would you guys like to tour


01:04:51.190 --> 01:04:52.559
the facilities yourselves?


01:04:52.594 --> 01:04:54.994
Oh, uh, I mean...


01:04:55.027 --> 01:04:56.664
uh, we could.


01:04:56.697 --> 01:04:58.532
- Yeah, why not?
- Great.


01:04:58.565 --> 01:05:01.001
I'll meet you guys at
the hyperloop, station three,


01:05:01.034 --> 01:05:03.137
in about 30 minutes.


01:05:03.170 --> 01:05:05.271
Elevators are down this hall.
Not-not those.


01:05:05.304 --> 01:05:07.173
Those lead you down
to the sublevels.


01:05:07.206 --> 01:05:09.376
You need special clearance
to get down there.


01:05:09.409 --> 01:05:12.045
- Oh, okay.
- 30 minutes.


01:05:20.588 --> 01:05:22.389
Here.


01:05:22.422 --> 01:05:24.056
Take this.


01:05:25.324 --> 01:05:27.494
- Okay?
- Yep.


01:05:37.070 --> 01:05:40.173
I'm really sorry
that it had to happen this way.


01:05:40.206 --> 01:05:42.476
Yep, that's what kidnappers say.


01:05:44.010 --> 01:05:45.646
Claire should never
have hidden you away.


01:05:45.679 --> 01:05:48.215
You're way too important,
Maisie.


01:05:52.119 --> 01:05:54.288
You took her, too.


01:05:55.289 --> 01:05:56.724
Yeah.


01:05:56.757 --> 01:05:59.527
We needed her
to help us understand you.


01:06:04.498 --> 01:06:06.500
Hey, Beta.


01:06:07.568 --> 01:06:09.335
You okay?


01:06:09.369 --> 01:06:10.637
Did you say "Beta"?


01:06:10.672 --> 01:06:12.338
Is that her name?


01:06:13.340 --> 01:06:14.608
I gave it to her.


01:06:14.641 --> 01:06:16.242
Beta's pretty special.


01:06:16.275 --> 01:06:19.346
You know, when we made Blue,
we used monitor lizard DNA


01:06:19.378 --> 01:06:22.181
to fill in the gaps
in her genome.


01:06:22.215 --> 01:06:25.152
Monitor lizards can reproduce
without a mate,


01:06:25.184 --> 01:06:29.121
so Beta and Blue
are genetically identical,


01:06:29.155 --> 01:06:31.224
and that's what they have
in common with you and...


01:06:31.257 --> 01:06:33.126
Charlotte.


01:06:35.262 --> 01:06:37.331
What do you know
about Charlotte?


01:06:37.364 --> 01:06:39.099
She died.


01:06:39.733 --> 01:06:41.367
A long time ago.


01:06:42.202 --> 01:06:44.271
It broke my grandpa's heart.


01:06:45.773 --> 01:06:47.509
So he made me.


01:06:49.076 --> 01:06:51.311
No, Maisie, actually, he didn't.


01:06:53.648 --> 01:06:56.083
Charlotte made you.


01:06:58.418 --> 01:07:01.288
I'm so excited for everyone to
see what we've been doing here.


01:07:01.320 --> 01:07:04.626
There's new technology
being made, new science,


01:07:04.659 --> 01:07:06.561
like, every day almost.


01:07:06.594 --> 01:07:08.161
And it's great to be...


01:07:08.195 --> 01:07:09.731
it's great to be
in the center...


01:07:09.764 --> 01:07:11.398
center of that.


01:07:11.431 --> 01:07:15.802
Charlotte lived
on Site B with all of us.


01:07:15.836 --> 01:07:18.204
Till the storm.


01:07:18.237 --> 01:07:19.541
She loved dinosaurs.


01:07:19.574 --> 01:07:21.141
Charlotte, be careful.


01:07:21.173 --> 01:07:22.476
Yeah, I will.


01:07:22.510 --> 01:07:24.612
She grew up around scientists.


01:07:25.579 --> 01:07:28.114
Then, eventually...


01:07:28.750 --> 01:07:30.416
...she became one herself.


01:07:30.449 --> 01:07:32.452
A butterfly flew into
my office this morning.


01:07:32.485 --> 01:07:34.856
They say tiny things
have huge impacts,


01:07:34.889 --> 01:07:36.858
and I agree wholeheartedly.


01:07:36.891 --> 01:07:39.293
She was brilliant.


01:07:40.695 --> 01:07:42.597
In ways that I'll never be.


01:07:42.630 --> 01:07:44.164
In the metaphysics of identity,


01:07:44.197 --> 01:07:46.333
can a replica
truly be the original?


01:07:46.365 --> 01:07:50.336
And if it's possible,
what makes it so?


01:07:55.175 --> 01:07:57.244
I've lost my pen.


01:08:00.480 --> 01:08:01.715
Is that me?


01:08:01.748 --> 01:08:04.117
Yeah.


01:08:04.150 --> 01:08:05.820
Just like Blue,
Charlotte was able


01:08:05.853 --> 01:08:08.155
to have a child all by herself.


01:08:08.856 --> 01:08:12.626
She created you
with her own DNA.


01:08:13.628 --> 01:08:15.597
So I do have a mother.


01:08:15.630 --> 01:08:19.131
Your grandfather didn't want
anyone to know the truth.


01:08:19.166 --> 01:08:22.234
He was protecting her and you.


01:08:22.869 --> 01:08:24.505
And we're the same?


01:08:26.472 --> 01:08:27.341
You were.


01:08:27.373 --> 01:08:29.777
When you were a baby,
Charlotte started


01:08:29.810 --> 01:08:31.813
to show symptoms
of a genetic disorder.


01:08:31.845 --> 01:08:34.448
That's how she died.


01:08:34.480 --> 01:08:38.217
She didn't know she had it
until after you were born.


01:08:38.251 --> 01:08:40.287
Do I have it, too?


01:08:40.319 --> 01:08:41.354
No.


01:08:41.387 --> 01:08:43.757
She changed your DNA.


01:08:43.791 --> 01:08:46.627
She altered every cell
in your body


01:08:46.661 --> 01:08:48.695
to eradicate this disease.


01:08:48.729 --> 01:08:51.698
No one on earth has ever
known how to do that.


01:08:51.733 --> 01:08:53.667
She fixed me.


01:08:53.701 --> 01:08:56.703
Charlotte's discovery
is a part of you now.


01:08:58.672 --> 01:09:01.943
Your DNA could change the world.


01:09:01.975 --> 01:09:04.277
And I have to know
how she did it,


01:09:04.310 --> 01:09:06.648
but I just can't
replicate her work.


01:09:06.680 --> 01:09:08.347
If I could just study you


01:09:08.381 --> 01:09:11.752
and Beta, whose DNA
was never changed, I could...


01:09:13.954 --> 01:09:16.890
...fix a terrible mistake
that I've made.


01:09:16.923 --> 01:09:19.225
What kind of mistake?


01:09:26.967 --> 01:09:29.636
Sublevel six. Restricted.


01:09:33.841 --> 01:09:35.710
Thanks for coming.


01:09:40.313 --> 01:09:41.983
Which lab did Malcolm say?


01:09:42.015 --> 01:09:44.283
L4.


01:09:47.854 --> 01:09:50.256
This is it.


01:10:08.643 --> 01:10:12.680
Okay, get in,
get the sample and get out.


01:10:12.713 --> 01:10:13.980
And move slow.


01:10:14.015 --> 01:10:16.751
They can swarm at
the slightest disturbance.


01:10:40.908 --> 01:10:42.676
Orthoptera.


01:10:43.644 --> 01:10:45.613
Two weeks.


01:10:49.015 --> 01:10:51.018
Fully mature.


01:10:51.051 --> 01:10:52.753
This one.


01:10:54.689 --> 01:10:56.657
Ready? Easy.


01:11:00.994 --> 01:11:02.630
Okay.


01:11:02.662 --> 01:11:04.296
Go.


01:11:04.931 --> 01:11:06.365
What?


01:11:07.100 --> 01:11:08.869
Go get it.


01:11:10.671 --> 01:11:12.038
Is that necessary?


01:11:12.073 --> 01:11:14.708
What did you think
was gonna happen?


01:11:14.742 --> 01:11:15.976
I have to take a sample.


01:11:16.010 --> 01:11:17.677
We need concrete evidence.
This is it.


01:11:17.712 --> 01:11:19.881
Alan, you said
there was no time.


01:11:19.913 --> 01:11:21.381
Can you get it?


01:11:21.413 --> 01:11:23.618
Of course I can get it.


01:11:24.551 --> 01:11:27.354
Easy. -


01:11:27.988 --> 01:11:29.657
Watch its legs.


01:11:32.092 --> 01:11:33.795
Here we go.


01:11:35.595 --> 01:11:36.939
They're cell signaling
between them.


01:11:36.963 --> 01:11:38.032
This is not good, Ellie.


01:11:38.064 --> 01:11:39.399
Almost got it.


01:11:41.702 --> 01:11:44.337
How does she remain
an asset, Henry,


01:11:44.371 --> 01:11:46.073
if you're incriminating
both of us


01:11:46.106 --> 01:11:48.440
by showing her classified things
on the computer?


01:11:48.475 --> 01:11:49.710
Charlotte Lockwood believed


01:11:49.743 --> 01:11:51.344
the methods we used
at Jurassic Park


01:11:51.377 --> 01:11:53.345
could cure disease.


01:11:53.380 --> 01:11:54.681
She was right.


01:11:54.715 --> 01:11:57.083
Having filled the gaps
in Maisie's genome


01:11:57.118 --> 01:11:59.052
with altered DNA,


01:11:59.086 --> 01:12:00.654
she used a pathogen to deliver


01:12:00.688 --> 01:12:02.823
the repaired sequence
to every cell.


01:12:02.856 --> 01:12:05.091
If I can repurpose what she did,


01:12:05.126 --> 01:12:07.528
I could change the locusts' DNA,


01:12:07.561 --> 01:12:09.697
eradicating them
in a single generation.


01:12:09.729 --> 01:12:13.835
Maisie and the baby raptor
will provide the missing data.


01:12:20.640 --> 01:12:23.376
Hey, do you want
to get out of here?


01:12:26.445 --> 01:12:28.615
What the...?


01:12:29.516 --> 01:12:30.851
Got it.


01:12:35.021 --> 01:12:36.724
Go!


01:12:40.862 --> 01:12:42.863
They're everywhere!


01:12:42.896 --> 01:12:44.599
Help me! Oh, God!


01:12:44.631 --> 01:12:46.567
No!


01:12:48.636 --> 01:12:50.436
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!


01:12:55.743 --> 01:12:57.110
Maisie.


01:13:08.655 --> 01:13:10.524
Asset containment breach.


01:13:10.557 --> 01:13:12.560
Please remain at your stations.


01:13:14.060 --> 01:13:15.529
Asset containment breach.


01:13:15.563 --> 01:13:17.163
Please remain at your stations.


01:13:19.800 --> 01:13:22.603
Oh, my God! Oh, God, I can't
see! -Where's the key?


01:13:41.087 --> 01:13:42.923
You okay?


01:13:42.957 --> 01:13:44.658
Yeah.


01:13:44.692 --> 01:13:46.060
You?


01:13:46.092 --> 01:13:47.560
Yeah.


01:13:49.829 --> 01:13:51.430
Oh.


01:13:56.770 --> 01:14:01.141
You're Dr. Ellie Sattler
and Alan Grant.


01:14:01.175 --> 01:14:03.475
You were at Jurassic Park.


01:14:03.511 --> 01:14:05.546
What-what are you doing here?


01:14:05.578 --> 01:14:07.515
What? What...


01:14:07.547 --> 01:14:09.617
what are you doing here?


01:14:11.284 --> 01:14:13.554
I'm Maisie Lockwood.


01:14:21.828 --> 01:14:23.564
Um...


01:14:23.596 --> 01:14:26.734
Hey, we don't, uh...


01:14:26.766 --> 01:14:29.136
we're not...
we don't work for Biosyn.


01:14:29.170 --> 01:14:30.270
I can tell.


01:14:30.304 --> 01:14:31.838
We got to get out of here.


01:14:31.872 --> 01:14:32.974
Yeah, we should go.


01:14:48.588 --> 01:14:51.559
Okay, in and out...
we find your girl and go.


01:14:52.626 --> 01:14:54.261
Tower, this is N-141.


01:14:54.295 --> 01:14:56.006
Request to land for
a freight delivery. Over.


01:14:56.029 --> 01:14:58.599
Uh, N-141, negative.
We've been advised


01:14:58.631 --> 01:15:00.734
you're carrying
unauthorized passengers. Over.


01:15:00.768 --> 01:15:02.136
Copy that, tower.


01:15:02.168 --> 01:15:04.537
Be advised
shipment is perishable.


01:15:04.572 --> 01:15:05.872
We need immediate clearance.


01:15:05.905 --> 01:15:08.609
- It's an emergency. Over.
- There isn't... No.


01:15:08.641 --> 01:15:11.045
Uh, negative.
Return to point of origin.


01:15:11.078 --> 01:15:12.613
Uh, you seem to be breaking up.


01:15:12.645 --> 01:15:14.046
Are-are you hearing me
on your side?


01:15:16.216 --> 01:15:18.719
Nice try, Kayla.
They will down your bird.


01:15:19.353 --> 01:15:21.622
Who is this? Is this Denise?


01:15:21.654 --> 01:15:24.125
You do not want me to start
spilling secrets, Denise.


01:15:24.158 --> 01:15:25.893
You remember Dubrovnik.


01:15:27.261 --> 01:15:30.331
She's... Different Denise.


01:15:30.363 --> 01:15:32.666
In accounts.


01:15:39.340 --> 01:15:41.175
Talked to Santos.


01:15:41.207 --> 01:15:42.909
It's the girl's parents.


01:15:45.679 --> 01:15:47.981
Sh-Shut off the ADS.


01:15:48.015 --> 01:15:49.984
You sure?


01:15:50.016 --> 01:15:51.985
Uh-huh.


01:15:57.625 --> 01:15:59.260
What's that?


01:15:59.292 --> 01:16:01.261
Uh, that's the, uh...


01:16:01.295 --> 01:16:03.096
that's the aerial
deterrent system.


01:16:03.130 --> 01:16:04.331
Keeps the airborne life away.


01:16:04.364 --> 01:16:06.033
Why is it blinking?


01:16:06.067 --> 01:16:07.944
Because dead-ass Denise in
the tower just turned it off.


01:16:07.967 --> 01:16:09.737
We got to get out of
this airspace right now.


01:16:14.675 --> 01:16:17.677
- That's another plane, right?
- Not exactly.


01:16:20.648 --> 01:16:22.048
Is that a...


01:16:22.082 --> 01:16:23.751
<i>Quetzalcoatlus.</i>


01:16:23.783 --> 01:16:26.087
Late Cretaceous.
Should've stayed there.


01:16:32.126 --> 01:16:34.662
Okay. Okay.


01:16:34.694 --> 01:16:36.930
It's cool. We're good.
It's gone.


01:16:53.913 --> 01:16:55.381
This plane is going down.


01:16:55.416 --> 01:16:58.685
If you're going to eject,
you need to do it now.


01:16:58.719 --> 01:17:00.753
I only got one chair,
and she's in it.


01:17:00.787 --> 01:17:03.756
- You don't have parachutes?
- I wasn't expecting company.


01:17:11.431 --> 01:17:12.867
Claire.


01:17:12.899 --> 01:17:14.400
We got to get you
off this plane.


01:17:14.435 --> 01:17:15.903
What?


01:17:15.935 --> 01:17:17.279
Parachute is gonna open
automatically.


01:17:17.304 --> 01:17:18.414
If it doesn't,
you pull this lever.


01:17:18.439 --> 01:17:19.707
Do you understand me?


01:17:19.739 --> 01:17:21.274
Claire!


01:17:21.307 --> 01:17:22.943
If it doesn't open
automatically,


01:17:22.976 --> 01:17:24.753
you're gonna pull this lever
here behind you, okay?


01:17:24.778 --> 01:17:26.814
- 10,000 feet!
- Hey.


01:17:26.846 --> 01:17:28.324
You're the one who's got to go
to get to her.


01:17:28.349 --> 01:17:30.783
You're her mom.
You're her only shot.


01:17:33.319 --> 01:17:35.756
I'll see you again.


01:17:36.457 --> 01:17:38.958
I love you.


01:18:27.474 --> 01:18:28.475
What's the plan?


01:18:28.510 --> 01:18:30.310
Whatever happens.


01:18:30.344 --> 01:18:32.145
That's the plan.


01:18:45.826 --> 01:18:47.461
- Three.
- That's it.


01:18:47.493 --> 01:18:49.363
Alan, we need the code.


01:18:49.395 --> 01:18:50.764
Let's try this thing.


01:18:50.797 --> 01:18:51.998
Yeah.


01:18:52.032 --> 01:18:54.001
Get down.


01:18:59.405 --> 01:19:01.108
- Thank God it's you.
- I don't know...


01:19:01.140 --> 01:19:03.109
This place is such a maze.


01:19:03.143 --> 01:19:04.521
- We were so confused.
- It's good you're here.


01:19:04.546 --> 01:19:06.021
But I thought
we were straight-up lost,


01:19:06.046 --> 01:19:07.524
then you said station three,
and I was like...


01:19:07.548 --> 01:19:09.426
- We thought you said...
- Do you have the sample?


01:19:09.449 --> 01:19:11.784
- What?
- What are you talking about?


01:19:11.819 --> 01:19:13.253
The DNA sample... do you have it?


01:19:13.287 --> 01:19:16.023
Biosyn's responsible
for the locust epidemic.


01:19:16.055 --> 01:19:17.791
Dodgson's covering it up.
You were right.


01:19:17.824 --> 01:19:19.859
I'm-I'm here to help you.


01:19:19.893 --> 01:19:21.462
Do you have it?


01:19:21.494 --> 01:19:23.096
- Uh...
- Yeah.


01:19:23.130 --> 01:19:24.163
Good.


01:19:25.198 --> 01:19:26.842
This pod will take you
straight to the airfield.


01:19:26.867 --> 01:19:28.435
We have a plane ready to fly.


01:19:28.469 --> 01:19:30.136
Ian told you
about Hexapod Allies?


01:19:30.170 --> 01:19:32.273
No. I told him.


01:19:32.305 --> 01:19:33.873
What?


01:19:33.907 --> 01:19:36.143
- Okay, you guys got to go.
- Wait.


01:19:39.912 --> 01:19:41.914
Maisie.


01:19:45.185 --> 01:19:46.386
Maisie Lockwood.


01:19:49.390 --> 01:19:50.923
Go.


01:24:05.177 --> 01:24:07.146
That was my baby.


01:24:15.255 --> 01:24:17.524
Where'd you learn to fly?


01:24:17.559 --> 01:24:19.493
Uh, Air Force.


01:24:19.527 --> 01:24:20.828
Legacy on my mama's side.


01:24:20.862 --> 01:24:22.596
Yeah. I'm Navy.


01:24:23.462 --> 01:24:25.431
And so, how'd you end up
doing this?


01:24:25.465 --> 01:24:27.702
I was a legit contract pilot
for a grip,


01:24:27.734 --> 01:24:29.235
but didn't exactly pay enough


01:24:29.269 --> 01:24:30.780
to be out here
and send the money home,


01:24:30.805 --> 01:24:33.707
so I hit up a few contacts for
the more lucrative shady shit.


01:24:35.341 --> 01:24:37.712
Honestly, I might be done
with this line of work.


01:24:37.744 --> 01:24:39.613
Is that why you're helping us?


01:24:42.750 --> 01:24:46.086
I was there when they handed
your girl off to Biosyn.


01:24:46.887 --> 01:24:50.323
I could've said something,
but I didn't.


01:24:50.356 --> 01:24:52.560
And when I saw her picture...


01:24:54.427 --> 01:24:56.496
It isn't enough to do nothing.


01:25:01.703 --> 01:25:03.369
Thank you.


01:25:49.650 --> 01:25:51.551
No.


01:25:55.823 --> 01:25:56.858
Nope.


01:26:20.981 --> 01:26:23.250
What an asshole.


01:27:13.900 --> 01:27:15.368
You good?


01:27:15.402 --> 01:27:16.871
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.


01:27:16.904 --> 01:27:18.337
Yeah, I'm not shook at all. You?


01:27:18.371 --> 01:27:20.574
Nah. Nah, no.


01:27:22.309 --> 01:27:24.277
The ejection seat beacon.


01:27:24.310 --> 01:27:26.847
- We'll find her.
- Okay. Okay.


01:27:26.881 --> 01:27:28.783
You really love her, huh?


01:27:30.051 --> 01:27:31.819
Yeah.


01:27:31.853 --> 01:27:33.554
I get it.


01:27:34.421 --> 01:27:36.524
I like redheads, too.


01:27:37.524 --> 01:27:39.060
What? God.


01:27:42.563 --> 01:27:43.296
Who is that?


01:27:43.329 --> 01:27:45.498
It's Grant and Sattler.


01:27:45.533 --> 01:27:47.635
- Is this live?
- 12 minutes ago.


01:27:47.667 --> 01:27:49.435
We were tracking
the escaped asset.


01:27:49.469 --> 01:27:50.704
Our guys missed it.


01:27:50.738 --> 01:27:52.873
They stole a DNA sample.


01:27:53.807 --> 01:27:55.909
- How'd they get in there?
- They used an access key.


01:27:55.943 --> 01:27:58.078
Yankee White clearance.


01:27:58.112 --> 01:28:00.081
One of our cameras
saw Ian Malcolm


01:28:00.113 --> 01:28:02.649
put something
in Sattler's pocket.


01:28:02.682 --> 01:28:04.786
All right.


01:28:04.819 --> 01:28:06.087
I want to see him.


01:28:06.119 --> 01:28:08.890
And get Ramsay up here,
too, will you?


01:28:08.922 --> 01:28:10.323
Where are they now?


01:28:10.356 --> 01:28:12.359
On the way to the airfield.


01:28:12.391 --> 01:28:14.561
They caught the hyperloop
right on schedule.


01:28:20.701 --> 01:28:22.537
How are you?


01:28:22.569 --> 01:28:24.639
You all right?


01:28:25.438 --> 01:28:27.340
Not really, no.


01:28:28.943 --> 01:28:30.811
Hey.


01:28:30.845 --> 01:28:33.581
I, uh, knew your mom.


01:28:36.783 --> 01:28:37.918
You did?


01:28:37.952 --> 01:28:39.686
Mm-hmm.


01:28:40.720 --> 01:28:44.524
Yeah, a few years
after Hammond died,


01:28:44.559 --> 01:28:48.563
she came to my university
to lecture, and...


01:28:48.595 --> 01:28:50.698
we became good friends.


01:28:50.730 --> 01:28:52.632
What was she like?


01:28:52.667 --> 01:28:53.734
Brilliant.


01:28:53.768 --> 01:28:55.837
Light-years ahead
of everybody else.


01:28:57.404 --> 01:28:58.840
And she had a conscience.


01:28:58.872 --> 01:29:01.440
While they were out
building theme parks,


01:29:01.474 --> 01:29:03.077
well, she was
determined to prove


01:29:03.109 --> 01:29:05.613
that genetic power
could save lives.


01:29:06.814 --> 01:29:08.582
And I was her experiment.


01:29:08.615 --> 01:29:09.917
No.


01:29:11.786 --> 01:29:13.921
She wanted a child
more than anything.


01:29:14.855 --> 01:29:18.457
But she wanted you to have
what she couldn't.


01:29:19.092 --> 01:29:20.962
A full life.


01:29:23.631 --> 01:29:25.800
I didn't know her long.


01:29:26.667 --> 01:29:28.903
But I know
she loved you very much.


01:29:49.055 --> 01:29:50.725
What's happening?


01:29:55.529 --> 01:29:57.899
This must be
the old amber mines.


01:29:58.932 --> 01:30:02.737
They must have made access doors
when they built these tunnels.


01:30:26.860 --> 01:30:28.194
Hey.


01:30:28.229 --> 01:30:30.664
I heard the alarm.
Everything all right?


01:30:30.698 --> 01:30:33.067
Yeah, no, no.
Nothing we can't, uh, handle.


01:30:33.100 --> 01:30:34.935
- Listen...
- You rang?


01:30:34.969 --> 01:30:36.770
Oh, good. Dr. Malcolm.


01:30:36.804 --> 01:30:38.939
You are... fired.


01:30:38.972 --> 01:30:40.573
What?


01:30:40.608 --> 01:30:43.810
It was such a cushy gig.


01:30:43.844 --> 01:30:47.081
You can, uh, give
your access key to security,


01:30:47.113 --> 01:30:48.815
if you still have it.


01:30:48.849 --> 01:30:50.260
One of the hyperloop pods just
shut down in the amber mines.


01:30:50.283 --> 01:30:51.985
What?


01:30:52.987 --> 01:30:55.221
Wow. This day.


01:30:55.256 --> 01:30:57.224
Uh, which... which pod are we...


01:30:57.257 --> 01:30:59.225
Are there, um...


01:30:59.260 --> 01:31:01.127
dinosaurs in the mines?


01:31:01.162 --> 01:31:02.762
There are dinosaurs everywhere.


01:31:02.796 --> 01:31:04.073
I mean, you know, technically,
birds are dinosaurs.


01:31:04.097 --> 01:31:05.565
Ge-Genetically speaking...


01:31:05.599 --> 01:31:06.976
Okay, Lewis, Grant and Sattler
are in this pod.


01:31:07.001 --> 01:31:08.841
We need to send
a security team out there ASAP.


01:31:08.868 --> 01:31:10.770
Okay. Absolutely, Ramsay.
Thank you.


01:31:10.805 --> 01:31:12.840
Uh, let's all just stay
in our lanes, though.


01:31:12.872 --> 01:31:14.975
We can take care of it.
Thank you, Doctor.


01:31:15.009 --> 01:31:17.645
That's it, huh?
Nothing else to see here?


01:31:17.677 --> 01:31:20.914
Uh, I'm not sure I admire
your tone right now.


01:31:20.948 --> 01:31:23.250
- You need to leave.
- Yeah, I do.


01:31:23.283 --> 01:31:26.787
But first, I owe
all these folks an apology.


01:31:26.820 --> 01:31:29.122
I think that by lending
my cachet to this joint


01:31:29.155 --> 01:31:30.890
I might have made it seem as if


01:31:30.925 --> 01:31:32.592
Biosyn wasn't
rotten to the core.


01:31:32.626 --> 01:31:33.761
That's enough, Ian.


01:31:33.793 --> 01:31:35.128
See, here's how they get you.


01:31:35.162 --> 01:31:36.305
They give you so many promotions


01:31:36.329 --> 01:31:37.965
in a short period of time


01:31:37.998 --> 01:31:39.876
that it bludgeons your capacity
for critical thinking.


01:31:39.899 --> 01:31:42.737
Oh, my God. -So then there are
doors that you don't open,


01:31:42.770 --> 01:31:44.204
things that you ignore.


01:31:44.238 --> 01:31:49.743
But mainly, he's exploiting
your enchantment with these.


01:31:49.777 --> 01:31:51.811
Is there an actual concern
here, or are you just...


01:31:51.845 --> 01:31:54.215
You're racing toward
the extinction of our species,


01:31:54.247 --> 01:31:55.949
and you don't care.


01:31:55.983 --> 01:31:58.985
You know exactly what you're
doing, but you won't stop.


01:31:59.020 --> 01:32:00.287
You can't.


01:32:00.320 --> 01:32:02.189
You know, I thought
you might be different,


01:32:02.222 --> 01:32:03.724
but you're just like
everyone else.


01:32:03.757 --> 01:32:05.158
You see what you want to see.


01:32:05.192 --> 01:32:08.128
You imagine unchecked avarice,


01:32:08.162 --> 01:32:09.930
so that's what you find.


01:32:09.963 --> 01:32:13.234
You envision what,
an evil, unbound Prometheus?


01:32:13.266 --> 01:32:14.769
So that's what I am to you?


01:32:14.801 --> 01:32:16.302
Prometheus got gored.


01:32:16.337 --> 01:32:18.872
So will you,
you rapacious rat bastard.


01:32:18.905 --> 01:32:23.144
Ramsay, would you help
Dr. Malcolm gather his things?


01:32:24.078 --> 01:32:26.713
His room, and then
to the airfield. That's it.


01:32:36.023 --> 01:32:37.690
Dodgson.


01:33:41.287 --> 01:33:43.090
Oh, God.


01:34:10.783 --> 01:34:12.920
<i>Allosaurus?</i>


01:34:14.154 --> 01:34:15.855
<i>Giganotosaurus.</i>


01:34:15.890 --> 01:34:17.925
Largest known
terrestrial carnivore.


01:34:18.859 --> 01:34:21.028
You put two apex predators
in one valley,


01:34:21.060 --> 01:34:23.329
pretty soon there's only
gonna be one.


01:34:54.494 --> 01:34:56.796
Did you feel that?


01:34:58.265 --> 01:34:59.966
That's an air current.


01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:02.101
There must be
an opening up ahead.


01:35:03.002 --> 01:35:05.206
How old is this mine,
do you think?


01:35:05.238 --> 01:35:06.974
Just breathe.


01:35:07.006 --> 01:35:09.176
Nobody panic.
Just watch out for bats.


01:35:09.210 --> 01:35:11.078
- Who said anything about bats?
- I hate bats.


01:35:11.110 --> 01:35:14.148
Well, there's probably no bats,
no falling rocks.


01:35:14.180 --> 01:35:15.949
Just the possibility
of toxic gas,


01:35:15.983 --> 01:35:17.417
dehydration, hypothermia.


01:35:17.451 --> 01:35:19.485
Just possibilities,
nothing for certain.


01:35:19.520 --> 01:35:21.387
Oh, I should've
left you where you were.


01:35:21.421 --> 01:35:23.224
- Why did I bring you into this?
- What?


01:35:23.256 --> 01:35:25.359
You were happy
in your element. -What?


01:35:25.391 --> 01:35:27.194
- Ellie.
- What?


01:35:27.228 --> 01:35:29.128
I wasn't happy.


01:35:30.130 --> 01:35:31.832
You weren't?


01:35:31.864 --> 01:35:33.867
- Do you guys have kids?
- What?


01:35:33.900 --> 01:35:35.537
Uh...


01:35:35.569 --> 01:35:37.270
No, I-I do.


01:35:37.304 --> 01:35:38.404
Two.


01:35:38.439 --> 01:35:39.907
But not with him?


01:35:41.408 --> 01:35:43.243
Uh...


01:35:43.277 --> 01:35:45.145
no.


01:35:45.179 --> 01:35:47.780
No, just old friends.


01:35:47.814 --> 01:35:50.984
Just old friends.


01:35:51.018 --> 01:35:53.052
Really?


01:35:57.224 --> 01:35:59.158
Won't be long before
security knows you're gone.


01:35:59.193 --> 01:36:01.795
Oh, a map.
That looks like an old map.


01:36:01.828 --> 01:36:02.796
You don't have a new map?


01:36:02.829 --> 01:36:04.030
There's an access gate


01:36:04.064 --> 01:36:05.533
at the northeast corner
of the mine.


01:36:05.567 --> 01:36:06.842
- If your friends make it out...
- If?


01:36:06.867 --> 01:36:08.301
When they make it out...


01:36:08.335 --> 01:36:10.136
- Yes, sir.
- ...that's where they'll be.


01:36:10.170 --> 01:36:13.207
These roads are protected,
right?


01:36:13.239 --> 01:36:14.841
Uh, yeah. I'd drive fast.


01:36:25.452 --> 01:36:27.320
You did good.


01:36:27.354 --> 01:36:28.889
Uh, yeah, well, actually,


01:36:28.921 --> 01:36:31.190
it's a complete disaster,
but thanks.


01:36:32.192 --> 01:36:33.293
Not yet.


01:36:44.070 --> 01:36:45.972
Watch yourself.


01:37:04.591 --> 01:37:06.993
- Ellie.
- Yeah.


01:37:11.497 --> 01:37:13.266
What was that?


01:37:19.472 --> 01:37:21.108
Be careful.


01:37:35.956 --> 01:37:37.796
- Oh, my God, Alan.
- Oh, my God. Are you okay?


01:37:55.475 --> 01:37:57.010
Forget the hat!


01:37:57.712 --> 01:38:00.079
Come on!


01:38:07.320 --> 01:38:08.921
Go, go, go!


01:38:09.556 --> 01:38:11.425
Go, go, go, go, go!


01:38:15.630 --> 01:38:17.197
It's a car.


01:38:18.966 --> 01:38:21.001
- Oh, my God. Ian!
- Ian, over here!


01:38:22.368 --> 01:38:24.203
- Please, Ian!
- Open the gate.


01:38:24.238 --> 01:38:25.672
Please help us.


01:38:25.707 --> 01:38:27.306
Do you know the code?


01:38:27.341 --> 01:38:29.309
I didn't know there was
gonna be a code.


01:38:30.042 --> 01:38:32.045
I didn't know there was
gonna be a code.


01:38:32.078 --> 01:38:34.515
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.


01:38:36.015 --> 01:38:37.984
The brake! Pull the brake!


01:38:38.018 --> 01:38:39.686
There are 10,000 possibilities.


01:38:39.720 --> 01:38:42.155
Push your legs against it!


01:38:42.189 --> 01:38:44.992
- 1984.
- Come on, Ian!


01:38:45.024 --> 01:38:47.127
Kick up against it! -Hurry!


01:38:47.161 --> 01:38:51.297
Miles Davis's birthday... 0526.


01:38:55.502 --> 01:38:57.337
- Ian!
- Please, please.


01:38:57.371 --> 01:38:58.471
Do something!


01:38:58.505 --> 01:39:00.006
We're not gonna make it.


01:39:00.039 --> 01:39:02.208
Let's-let's all try
and stay positive.


01:39:18.257 --> 01:39:21.494
- Please.
- I know, I know, I know.


01:39:26.801 --> 01:39:29.136
Oh, my God! Close it!


01:39:30.637 --> 01:39:32.573
What do you know?
It actually worked.


01:39:37.243 --> 01:39:39.479
Ian, this is Maisie.


01:39:39.514 --> 01:39:41.314
Hi, Maisie.


01:39:41.347 --> 01:39:43.182
We got the DNA.


01:39:44.117 --> 01:39:45.485
We need to get out
of this valley.


01:39:45.520 --> 01:39:48.387
- Yeah. Let's go. Let's go.
- Come on. Come on.


01:40:19.286 --> 01:40:21.387
Come on. Come, come on.


01:41:30.625 --> 01:41:32.560
Go on, get!


01:41:32.594 --> 01:41:34.628
Yuck.


01:41:34.662 --> 01:41:36.597
- Oh, my God.
- Hey.


01:41:36.631 --> 01:41:38.832
Oh, my God.


01:41:38.865 --> 01:41:40.534
I thought you were dead.


01:41:40.568 --> 01:41:42.202
What do they even eat?


01:41:47.274 --> 01:41:49.242
We better get inside.


01:42:29.550 --> 01:42:31.451
Oh, go ahead.


01:43:09.856 --> 01:43:12.592
Containment chamber compromised.


01:43:28.509 --> 01:43:29.577
It's locked.


01:43:29.609 --> 01:43:32.378
Gonna need something heavy,
something sharp or both.


01:43:43.024 --> 01:43:46.460
That... can't be right.


01:43:57.872 --> 01:43:59.974
- Is that...?
- Oh, no.


01:44:00.006 --> 01:44:01.842
Oh, my God.


01:44:03.511 --> 01:44:05.444
He's burning the evidence.


01:44:06.713 --> 01:44:08.048
Oh, my God. Oh, my God!


01:44:08.082 --> 01:44:10.317
- Oh, my... Ew!
- That's bananas.


01:44:27.667 --> 01:44:28.569
Oh, my God.


01:44:28.603 --> 01:44:34.274
I-I-I know this may seem
precarious, but...


01:44:34.908 --> 01:44:36.475
No, we're-we're teetering.


01:44:38.813 --> 01:44:41.047
Should we all lean
to the left or something?


01:44:41.082 --> 01:44:42.792
That's very constructive.
Thank you, Maisie.


01:44:42.817 --> 01:44:44.918
Yeah.


01:44:44.952 --> 01:44:47.521
Slow. Slow.


01:44:48.655 --> 01:44:50.422
Slow.


01:44:52.592 --> 01:44:54.095
Yay.


01:44:54.127 --> 01:44:55.695
We're fine.


01:44:55.729 --> 01:44:57.532
- See this?
- Mm-hmm.


01:44:57.564 --> 01:44:59.431
- This is fine.
- Mm-hmm.


01:45:13.079 --> 01:45:14.649
Alan?


01:45:14.681 --> 01:45:16.117
Alan!


01:45:16.149 --> 01:45:17.752
How is everybody?


01:45:27.595 --> 01:45:29.930
It's my parents.


01:45:30.898 --> 01:45:32.465
Help!


01:45:32.498 --> 01:45:34.034
Help!


01:45:34.068 --> 01:45:35.467
Listen.


01:45:35.502 --> 01:45:38.371
Help! Help!


01:45:42.609 --> 01:45:44.712
Oh, my God.


01:45:44.744 --> 01:45:46.814
You're okay.


01:45:46.847 --> 01:45:48.615
You're okay.


01:45:48.649 --> 01:45:50.016
You came to get me, actually.


01:45:50.051 --> 01:45:51.384
- You came to get me.
- Yeah.


01:45:51.417 --> 01:45:53.554
Of course we did, sweetheart.


01:45:53.587 --> 01:45:55.823
- Heya, kid.
- Of course.


01:45:57.489 --> 01:45:59.527
I remember you.


01:46:00.161 --> 01:46:02.762
Remember you, too.


01:46:12.573 --> 01:46:14.542
They helped me escape.


01:46:14.574 --> 01:46:16.676
Yeah?


01:46:18.845 --> 01:46:20.747
You okay?


01:46:23.818 --> 01:46:25.653
- Thank you.
- Yeah.


01:46:28.055 --> 01:46:29.623
We got to go.


01:46:29.657 --> 01:46:32.693
Gonna have to break a window
to get inside that thing.


01:46:33.560 --> 01:46:35.863
Hope nobody's afraid of heights.


01:46:48.074 --> 01:46:50.443
Don't move.


01:47:08.595 --> 01:47:09.796
What is that?


01:47:09.829 --> 01:47:11.932
<i>Giganotosaurus.</i>


01:47:14.135 --> 01:47:16.604
Biggest carnivore
the world has ever seen.


01:47:34.988 --> 01:47:36.823
Maisie, Maisie, look at me.


01:47:36.856 --> 01:47:38.591
Look at me.


01:48:17.664 --> 01:48:19.734
- Go, go, go, go.
- Come on!


01:48:23.904 --> 01:48:26.774
No, no, no! No!


01:48:31.045 --> 01:48:32.912
- Hustle.
- I'm gonna die!


01:48:32.947 --> 01:48:34.748
- Climb. Climb, kid.
- No!


01:48:34.782 --> 01:48:37.551
- You're not. No, you're not.
- You're okay. -


01:48:45.658 --> 01:48:47.962
Go, go, go, go, go, go.


01:49:04.211 --> 01:49:06.113
Come on.


01:49:07.081 --> 01:49:08.783
Hey.


01:49:14.988 --> 01:49:16.990
Oh, yeah. Come here.


01:49:33.673 --> 01:49:36.010
- Go, go, go.
- Help me open it. Help me out.


01:49:40.247 --> 01:49:42.216
I got ya.


01:49:43.317 --> 01:49:44.952
Go, go, go.


01:49:44.984 --> 01:49:46.720
Go, go, go, go, go!


01:49:49.122 --> 01:49:50.157
Run.


01:50:06.940 --> 01:50:08.876
See? Not so bad.


01:50:15.181 --> 01:50:16.417
Come on.


01:50:18.152 --> 01:50:19.886
Claire!


01:51:01.729 --> 01:51:03.697
Call an evacuation.


01:51:03.730 --> 01:51:05.765
We need to bring
the animals inside.


01:51:05.798 --> 01:51:07.768
The regulations are clear
that in the event


01:51:07.801 --> 01:51:09.936
- of a level two...
- Shh!


01:51:11.104 --> 01:51:12.840
Jeffrey.


01:51:18.045 --> 01:51:19.846
God...


01:51:19.880 --> 01:51:21.814
- ...damn it!
- Oh.


01:51:23.149 --> 01:51:25.418
Just...


01:51:25.452 --> 01:51:26.953
Just call it.


01:51:26.987 --> 01:51:29.088
Attention, attention.


01:51:29.122 --> 01:51:31.457
This is an immediate
evacuation order.


01:51:31.492 --> 01:51:33.793
Remote herding system
is now active.


01:51:33.827 --> 01:51:37.198
All living assets en route
to emergency containment.


01:51:59.886 --> 01:52:02.922
Can't get hold of anybody
since everything is, uh,


01:52:02.957 --> 01:52:04.225
on fire.


01:52:04.257 --> 01:52:06.961
- Dr. Sattler, get some water.
- Oh. Thanks.


01:52:06.993 --> 01:52:09.229
Dr. Grant? Here you are.


01:52:09.262 --> 01:52:10.930
I'm, uh... I'm Owen Grady.


01:52:10.965 --> 01:52:12.533
Big fan. I read your book.


01:52:12.567 --> 01:52:14.268
Well, book on tape.


01:52:14.301 --> 01:52:16.537
Owen Grady, Owen Grady.


01:52:16.570 --> 01:52:18.838
Yeah, I know who you are.


01:52:18.872 --> 01:52:21.509
- You trained raptors.
- Yeah.


01:52:21.542 --> 01:52:23.777
I tried. Yeah.


01:52:23.810 --> 01:52:25.112
How you doing?


01:52:25.145 --> 01:52:26.980
The one here.


01:52:27.014 --> 01:52:28.983
You, uh... you were at
Jurassic World.


01:52:29.015 --> 01:52:30.518
Jurassic World?


01:52:30.551 --> 01:52:33.319
Not a fan. Mm-mm.


01:52:34.220 --> 01:52:36.923
Okay, so we good to find
a way out of here?


01:52:36.957 --> 01:52:37.858
Yep.


01:52:37.890 --> 01:52:39.393
Let's get it.


01:52:39.426 --> 01:52:42.895
There's a helicopter
out in the main complex.


01:52:42.930 --> 01:52:45.231
We turn the ADS back on,
we go home.


01:52:45.265 --> 01:52:48.269
- Wait, what's an ADS?
- Aerial deterrent system.


01:52:48.301 --> 01:52:49.837
Oh, uh...


01:52:49.869 --> 01:52:52.139
You know,
for the pterodactyls and shit.


01:52:52.171 --> 01:52:53.551
Keeps them away
from the helicopters.


01:52:53.574 --> 01:52:55.876
Well, how do we turn it back on?


01:52:55.908 --> 01:52:57.511
Okay, it looks like
all the systems


01:52:57.545 --> 01:52:59.012
run through to the control room,


01:52:59.046 --> 01:53:00.413
which is on the third floor.


01:53:00.447 --> 01:53:01.981
Oh.


01:53:02.015 --> 01:53:04.184
These outposts are all
connected underground.


01:53:09.422 --> 01:53:11.358
All right, easy, Rambo.


01:53:21.636 --> 01:53:24.070
So you worked
in the raptor pen, huh?


01:53:24.904 --> 01:53:26.608
- Yeah.
- Wow, and what-what happens?


01:53:26.640 --> 01:53:29.176
Do you just tell 'em what
to do, and they, uh...


01:53:29.208 --> 01:53:31.311
they comply or...?


01:53:31.345 --> 01:53:35.282
Well, it's a human/animal bond
based on mutual respect.


01:53:35.315 --> 01:53:37.519
Mm-hmm.


01:53:37.551 --> 01:53:40.054
Had a dog once.


01:53:40.087 --> 01:53:44.525
Humped my leg so much, I...
I got a callous on my shinbone.


01:53:44.559 --> 01:53:46.327
That's a true story.


01:53:58.640 --> 01:54:00.341
Oh, God.


01:54:00.373 --> 01:54:02.842
Hey. Good.


01:54:03.511 --> 01:54:05.011
Here's what I'm thinking.


01:54:05.045 --> 01:54:07.948
We get started again,
you and me.


01:54:07.980 --> 01:54:10.250
I can get money.


01:54:11.085 --> 01:54:12.453
Yeah, money's cheap these days.


01:54:12.485 --> 01:54:13.886
What-what's the matter?


01:54:13.921 --> 01:54:15.988
Don't look so worried.
There's...


01:54:16.023 --> 01:54:18.125
There's opportunity
in everything.


01:54:18.158 --> 01:54:20.394
E-Even this.
You'll-you'll learn that.


01:54:20.426 --> 01:54:22.261
I've been thinking, um...


01:54:23.130 --> 01:54:24.997
Maybe you take more
of a lead now, okay?


01:54:25.032 --> 01:54:27.434
You're ready, I think.


01:54:27.467 --> 01:54:29.002
Here, take...


01:54:29.036 --> 01:54:31.070
What the hell is
the matter with you?


01:54:40.180 --> 01:54:41.414
It was you.


01:54:42.416 --> 01:54:45.018
You told Malcolm about
the program. You-you...


01:54:45.720 --> 01:54:49.088
You set this whole thing up?
You set me up?


01:54:49.122 --> 01:54:51.658
I gave you every opportunity
I did not have. I...


01:54:53.159 --> 01:54:55.996
We have an understanding,
Ramsay,


01:54:56.029 --> 01:54:58.164
and you do not break that.


01:55:00.466 --> 01:55:02.435
I would not break this.


01:55:05.405 --> 01:55:07.173
I'm not you.


01:55:21.588 --> 01:55:24.091
Oh, this is very bad.


01:55:25.324 --> 01:55:27.561
This is the same system
we used at the park.


01:55:27.595 --> 01:55:30.264
Great, so we can, uh,
turn on the...


01:55:30.296 --> 01:55:32.498
the thing, and then we all
get out of here?


01:55:32.533 --> 01:55:34.467
Let's see. ADS...


01:55:35.335 --> 01:55:38.037
What's this?
What-what's error 99?


01:55:38.070 --> 01:55:39.405
Not enough power.


01:55:39.439 --> 01:55:41.708
In a breakdown,
all available power is seized


01:55:41.743 --> 01:55:43.744
by the primary system
to keep running.


01:55:43.778 --> 01:55:45.579
We need all that power
to reactivate the ADS.


01:55:45.613 --> 01:55:48.047
So the system's safety feature
is what's gonna kill us?


01:55:48.081 --> 01:55:50.283
- Of course.
- How do we get more power?


01:55:50.317 --> 01:55:52.462
Uh, well, we can't, but we can
redistribute what we have


01:55:52.485 --> 01:55:54.054
if we just... just need to...


01:55:54.087 --> 01:55:55.322
Shut down the primary system.


01:55:55.354 --> 01:55:57.090
- Yes, exactly.
- Where is it?


01:55:57.123 --> 01:55:58.702
- Uh, next floor up.
- I'm coming with you.


01:55:58.725 --> 01:56:00.359
We escaped down here.


01:56:01.261 --> 01:56:02.739
Where is that?
Water treatment center.


01:56:02.764 --> 01:56:05.064
Hydroelectric system...
sub eight.


01:56:05.097 --> 01:56:06.734
Give me eight minutes,
I could find her.


01:56:06.768 --> 01:56:09.101
- Wait, who's this now?
- Beta.


01:56:09.136 --> 01:56:11.104
- Blue's baby.
- Velociraptor.


01:56:11.137 --> 01:56:13.239
- What?
- A baby raptor?


01:56:13.273 --> 01:56:15.074
And you gave her a name.
How about that?


01:56:15.108 --> 01:56:17.010
I made a promise
we would bring her home.


01:56:17.043 --> 01:56:20.012
You made a promise
to a dinosaur.


01:56:20.046 --> 01:56:21.615
You're coming with us, right?


01:56:21.649 --> 01:56:23.417
Maisie, I...


01:56:23.449 --> 01:56:24.519
Please.


01:56:27.421 --> 01:56:28.756
I'll be on channel five.


01:56:28.789 --> 01:56:30.490
- Okay.
- We're on three.


01:56:32.259 --> 01:56:33.528
Come back.


01:56:34.529 --> 01:56:35.996
I always come back.


01:56:37.163 --> 01:56:40.000
I'll have that chopper hot
in ten. Wait for my signal.


01:56:41.368 --> 01:56:43.770
Evacuation phase four complete.


01:56:43.805 --> 01:56:46.273
All living assets
now in containment.


01:56:54.815 --> 01:56:56.283
Come on.


01:57:08.328 --> 01:57:10.329
Still get nightmares?


01:57:10.363 --> 01:57:12.567
All the time.


01:57:12.600 --> 01:57:14.268
You?


01:57:15.101 --> 01:57:16.804
I have a lot of regrets.


01:57:16.837 --> 01:57:18.471
Oh, yeah?


01:57:19.606 --> 01:57:21.274
Well...


01:57:21.307 --> 01:57:25.145
we hold on to regret,
we stay in the past.


01:57:27.881 --> 01:57:30.250
What matters, I guess, is...


01:57:31.484 --> 01:57:33.287
...is what we do now.


01:57:33.319 --> 01:57:34.453
Right?


01:57:34.488 --> 01:57:35.657
Yeah.


01:57:52.907 --> 01:57:55.274
Nobody said there'd be bugs.


01:57:56.877 --> 01:57:59.713
B4. She's in here.


01:57:59.747 --> 01:58:01.716
Watch the sides.


01:58:01.748 --> 01:58:04.451
They always come from the sides.


01:58:05.752 --> 01:58:08.890
You know, at first we thought...


01:58:08.922 --> 01:58:12.560
they disembowel their prey,
but no.


01:58:12.594 --> 01:58:16.128
They're smart enough to go
straight for the throat.


01:58:16.162 --> 01:58:18.497
The veins, the arteries.


01:58:19.365 --> 01:58:21.201
Sometimes both at the same time.


01:58:21.234 --> 01:58:22.604
Okay.


01:58:22.636 --> 01:58:25.137
Oh, okay.


01:58:25.171 --> 01:58:26.273
We've got you.


01:58:26.305 --> 01:58:27.742
It's right down that aisle.


01:58:27.774 --> 01:58:30.143
It's right down that aisle
where you are. -


01:58:30.176 --> 01:58:31.746
Why are they skulking in-in...


01:58:31.779 --> 01:58:32.890
You can sprint right for it.


01:58:32.913 --> 01:58:35.414
Okay. Here it is.


01:58:35.448 --> 01:58:37.528
Okay, so it-it'll be a yellow
button on a grid of six.


01:58:37.551 --> 01:58:39.886
There's a green button.
Do you see a green button?


01:58:39.921 --> 01:58:41.287
It's not that green button.


01:58:41.320 --> 01:58:42.533
- It's four...
- which one's the button?


01:58:42.556 --> 01:58:43.323
Four from the bottom.


01:58:43.356 --> 01:58:44.759
- Above the...
- Whoa, whoa.


01:58:44.792 --> 01:58:46.292
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Fourth one up?


01:58:46.326 --> 01:58:47.805
Third one down
or fourth one up... same thing.


01:58:47.828 --> 01:58:49.395
Ian, be specific.


01:58:53.967 --> 01:58:55.703
She was here.


01:58:55.737 --> 01:58:57.572
Lights off.


01:59:03.677 --> 01:59:05.779
I don't know how I could
possibly be more specific


01:59:05.813 --> 01:59:08.815
other than to say that the one
you want is marked with...


01:59:08.850 --> 01:59:10.652
- E1.
- E1. E1.


01:59:10.685 --> 01:59:13.420
E1.


01:59:14.421 --> 01:59:16.724
Yeah.


01:59:20.694 --> 01:59:23.195
No. No, no, no, no.


01:59:28.770 --> 01:59:31.538
Damn it, she's fast.


01:59:33.908 --> 01:59:34.908
Hey.


01:59:36.010 --> 01:59:37.645
Eyes on me.


01:59:41.314 --> 01:59:44.350
I've got to hit her
on the side of her neck.


01:59:44.384 --> 01:59:46.720
Maisie, you're gonna
hold her focus.


01:59:46.753 --> 01:59:49.657
Grant, we're triangulating.


01:59:55.563 --> 01:59:56.663
Go.


02:00:25.425 --> 02:00:27.226
Sorry, girl.


02:00:27.962 --> 02:00:30.329
I promised your mom
I'd get you home.


02:00:31.331 --> 02:00:33.332
Primary system rebooting.


02:00:33.365 --> 02:00:34.511
Wait. Whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa.


02:00:34.534 --> 02:00:35.737
- No, no, no.
- No, no, no.


02:00:35.770 --> 02:00:36.871
It's rebooting.


02:00:36.904 --> 02:00:38.144
No, it shouldn't be doing that.


02:00:49.917 --> 02:00:51.652
Here, take this.


02:01:07.501 --> 02:01:08.811
- We got to stay on it.
- Ian, shut it down!


02:01:08.836 --> 02:01:10.369
We're-we're gonna make it work.


02:01:10.403 --> 02:01:11.480
We're gonna figure this out.
It's very complex.


02:01:11.505 --> 02:01:13.573
We don't have time for complex!


02:01:18.411 --> 02:01:20.412
Primary system compromised.


02:01:22.984 --> 02:01:24.484
Wait a minute, wait a minute.


02:01:24.519 --> 02:01:25.787
Aerial deterrent system active.


02:01:25.819 --> 02:01:27.386
Victory! Victory!


02:01:30.957 --> 02:01:32.827
Damn, that felt good.


02:02:00.720 --> 02:02:03.658
Oh, come on!


02:02:54.774 --> 02:02:56.610
What's your story?


02:03:00.180 --> 02:03:01.882
Wait!


02:03:11.792 --> 02:03:13.994
At Biosyn, we're dedicated


02:03:14.028 --> 02:03:16.130
to the idea that dinosaurs


02:03:16.162 --> 02:03:18.832
can teach us more
about ourselves.


02:03:23.069 --> 02:03:25.972
All right,
Kayla, we're good to go.


02:03:36.050 --> 02:03:37.818
Okay, cutie.


02:03:43.256 --> 02:03:46.527
Oh, come here. Oh.


02:03:46.560 --> 02:03:47.761
- You all right?
- Someday.


02:03:47.795 --> 02:03:48.662
Okay.


02:03:48.695 --> 02:03:50.730
Hey.


02:03:57.971 --> 02:03:59.105
I remember you.


02:03:59.140 --> 02:04:01.242
Please, you have
to listen to me.


02:04:01.274 --> 02:04:03.243
You created
an ecological disaster.


02:04:03.277 --> 02:04:04.878
And I can fix it.


02:04:05.880 --> 02:04:09.550
Charlotte Lockwood changed
every cell in Maisie's body.


02:04:09.582 --> 02:04:11.085
It saved her life.


02:04:11.118 --> 02:04:15.088
If I can understand how
Charlotte rewrote Maisie's DNA,


02:04:15.122 --> 02:04:18.091
I can spread change from
one locust to the entire swarm


02:04:18.125 --> 02:04:20.460
before it's too late.


02:04:21.996 --> 02:04:24.966
It's okay. It's okay.


02:04:28.135 --> 02:04:30.502
It's what she would have wanted.


02:04:33.106 --> 02:04:34.774
Thank you.


02:04:34.809 --> 02:04:36.176
No, no, no.


02:04:36.210 --> 02:04:38.078
No, no, no, no, no.


02:04:38.112 --> 02:04:39.980
Him?


02:04:40.014 --> 02:04:41.247
Not him.


02:04:41.282 --> 02:04:42.984
Not him. It's always him.


02:04:43.016 --> 02:04:45.118
Every si...


02:04:45.152 --> 02:04:47.688
Is that a dinosaur
on your shoulder?


02:04:48.288 --> 02:04:50.489
Yeah. Why?


02:04:51.125 --> 02:04:53.060
I have air.
Meet me at the center.


02:04:53.094 --> 02:04:55.137
No, no, no, no, no, no.
W-Wait, wait, wait. Hey, hey.


02:04:55.162 --> 02:04:56.896
D-Do... do not land in here.


02:04:56.930 --> 02:04:58.608
I don't have a choice, dude.
The valley isn't safe.


02:04:58.631 --> 02:05:00.967
No, they're not
in the valley anymore!


02:05:02.036 --> 02:05:03.604
Oh!


02:06:33.226 --> 02:06:34.261
This isn't about us.


02:07:00.421 --> 02:07:02.222
Run!


02:07:05.725 --> 02:07:07.394
Oh, my God!
Get him up, get him up!


02:07:07.427 --> 02:07:09.729
- Come on, come on!
- Come on.


02:07:12.733 --> 02:07:14.453
Come on, come on,
come on, come on, come on.


02:07:18.338 --> 02:07:19.873
Come on!


02:07:33.487 --> 02:07:35.221
Ellie, no!


02:08:04.484 --> 02:08:06.220
Go on, Maisie! Go!


02:08:08.021 --> 02:08:09.422
- Ramsay, get in.
- You're in.


02:08:09.456 --> 02:08:11.692
Come on, come on,
come on, come on.


02:08:15.462 --> 02:08:17.965
Everybody hold on to somebody.


02:09:38.979 --> 02:09:40.780
Ow.


02:09:42.181 --> 02:09:43.884
No, at every level.


02:09:43.917 --> 02:09:46.386
Complete systemic corruption
in-in the executive ranks.


02:09:46.420 --> 02:09:48.921
"Systemic corruption."
You get that? Write that down.


02:09:50.323 --> 02:09:51.559
Yeah, it's crazy.


02:09:51.592 --> 02:09:53.894
Oh, and then...
and then we crashed


02:09:53.926 --> 02:09:55.296
into this ice lake, right?


02:09:55.328 --> 02:09:57.230
I mean, they literally
owe me a plane.


02:09:57.264 --> 02:10:00.100
I need to get this sample
vetted at the lab


02:10:00.134 --> 02:10:03.069
before I take it
to my contact at <i>The Times.</i>


02:10:04.639 --> 02:10:07.341
You could, uh, come with me.


02:10:08.609 --> 02:10:11.377
Unless you need
to get back to your dig.


02:10:13.913 --> 02:10:16.182
- Ellie.
- Yeah?


02:10:18.085 --> 02:10:20.220
I am coming with you.


02:10:30.096 --> 02:10:31.565
I know.


02:10:31.599 --> 02:10:33.000
One more minute,


02:10:33.033 --> 02:10:35.135
then we'll send you home
with your folks.


02:11:13.940 --> 02:11:16.210
<i>Today marks
the first day of testimony</i>


02:11:16.243 --> 02:11:18.546
<i>from Biosyn whistleblower
Ramsay Cole.</i>


02:11:18.579 --> 02:11:20.180
<i>The Senate will also hear from</i>


02:11:20.213 --> 02:11:22.550
<i>Doctors Grant, Sattler
and Malcolm,</i>


02:11:22.583 --> 02:11:24.150
<i>who have been vocal
in this debate</i>


02:11:24.184 --> 02:11:26.052
<i>since the incident
at Jurassic Park.</i>


02:11:28.689 --> 02:11:30.557
You look...


02:11:30.591 --> 02:11:32.893
- Uncomfortable.
- Trustworthy.


02:11:37.430 --> 02:11:40.266
Yeah. Not getting used to it.


02:11:42.034 --> 02:11:44.104
Let's finish this.


02:11:44.137 --> 02:11:45.238
Yeah.


02:11:49.309 --> 02:11:51.110
<i>Dr. Henry Wu has found</i>


02:11:51.145 --> 02:11:54.113
<i>an emergency solution
to the ecological crisis.</i>


02:11:54.148 --> 02:11:57.251
<i>His use of a pathogen
to alter the locusts' DNA</i>


02:11:57.283 --> 02:12:00.220
<i>has revolutionized
modern genetics.</i>


02:12:00.253 --> 02:12:03.122
<i>He attributed the discovery
to another scientist,</i>


02:12:03.157 --> 02:12:07.261
<i>Charlotte Lockwood,
who died nearly 13 years ago.</i>


02:12:34.354 --> 02:12:36.724
<i>By UN decree, Biosyn Valley</i>


02:12:36.757 --> 02:12:39.627
<i>has been designated
a global sanctuary.</i>


02:12:39.661 --> 02:12:41.695
<i>The animals
will live there free,</i>


02:12:41.729 --> 02:12:44.131
<i>safe from the outside world.</i>


02:12:48.167 --> 02:12:50.203
- Money?
- Money.


02:12:50.237 --> 02:12:52.005
Thank you.


02:14:54.628 --> 02:14:58.733
Life on Earth has existed for
hundreds of millions of years.


02:14:59.667 --> 02:15:02.402
And dinosaurs were only
a part of that,


02:15:02.435 --> 02:15:05.204
and we're an even smaller
part of that.


02:15:05.238 --> 02:15:07.708
They really put us
in perspective.


02:15:08.743 --> 02:15:10.845
<i>The idea that life on Earth</i>


02:15:10.877 --> 02:15:13.246
<i>existed 65 million years ago...</i>


02:15:14.280 --> 02:15:16.216
...it's humbling.


02:15:17.250 --> 02:15:19.485
We act like we're alone here,
but we're not.


02:15:19.520 --> 02:15:23.557
<i>We're part of a fragile system
made up of all living things.</i>


02:15:24.658 --> 02:15:28.630
<i>If we're going to survive,
we'll have to trust each other,</i>


02:15:28.662 --> 02:15:30.765
<i>depend on each other,</i>


02:15:30.797 --> 02:15:33.332
coexist.

